window.SEARCH = {"n1": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts arpasu de sus «the entry of the lord into jerusalem» – icon on glass. • “the icon does not belong to a single day in the calendar; it is a window always open to heaven. christ comes, meek and humble, to enter the jerusalem of our souls at every moment, bringing peace and blessing to the home that receives him.” • i am sharing with you a work just finished in our workshop, made with love and care on glass, in the established tradition of the transylvanian icon painters (after the traditional model from arpasu de sus). • unlike the works made to order, this icon is available and is looking for a home to bless. • if you would like this icon in your home, or would like to give it to someone dear, you can contact me privately for details. i wish you days full of quiet, peace and light in your soul!", "p699": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise nicula, 19th century ⊹“the table of paradise” or “the heavenly feast” in a small icon painted on glass, model: nicula, 19th century. a theme i have been asked for many, many times over the years.", "p700": "saint elijah the prophet sfantul proroc ilie saints and archangels early 19th century 20 july • 20 july: the romanian orthodox church celebrates the ascent into heaven of the holy great prophet elijah the tishbite, a saint honoured as a great wonderworker and bringer of rain in times of drought. • we welcome the great feast with an icon on glass, made after the icon «the ascent of the holy prophet elijah into heaven, with scenes from his life» (scheii brasovului, model from the early 19th century) • about the icon: • i painted this icon after a 19th-century transylvanian model, in the traditional technique. the icon shows the classic scene of saint elijah appearing in the chariot of fire. in the upper part, this chariot appears in the sky, drawn by two red winged horses. the saint stands in the chariot, holding the reins in one hand and in the other the whip with which he drives the horses. the chariot is surrounded by flames. in the lower part, on the ground, saint elijah is shown fed by the ravens, and elisha, with his hands joined in prayer, awaiting saint elijah's mantle. • many happy returns to all who celebrate their name day!🥀", "p705": "the burning bush of the mother of god rugul aprins al maicii domnului the mother of god “the burning bush of the theotokos” • this icon painted on glass is inspired by several depictions, one of them being the first such icon to reach our country (in the 1940s), at the antim monastery in bucharest. many generations of the church's servants and of the faithful have prayed before this icon at the antim monastery, and it also inspired the well-known hesychast movement “the burning bush”, a group that kept the fire of faith alive in the hearts of many romanians during the communist rule. • the icon “the burning bush” shows a large eight-pointed star in the form of overlapping rhombuses, with the mother of god holding the saviour in her arms at their centre. four of the eight points are red, representing the fire, and the other four, painted green, symbolise that the bush did not burn but remained whole. on the points of the red star are the symbols of the four holy evangelists: the angel (saint matthew), the lion (saint mark), the ox (saint luke) and the eagle (saint john), and on the four points of the green star the holy angels are depicted. • this icon is not available; it was sent to paris, with great joy.❤", "p706": "saint michael the archangel sfantul arhanghel mihail saints and archangels • the archangel michael🌿 and so the small icon (13x18 cm) was made, with joy.", "p708": "saint andrew the apostle sfantul apostol andrei saints and archangels ⊹saint andrew the apostle⊹ • father cleopa: “we romanians have a church of apostolic origin, founded in the first century after the ascension of the lord into heaven. saint andrew the apostle brought us to christianity and celebrated the first holy liturgy on romanian soil. he freed us from demons and passions and united us with christ through sacrifice and the liturgy. he taught us how to be saved through humility, through prayer and through love.” • the icon – my own composition – that i am showing you today is not available; it was ordered for a baptism, as a gift for a delightful newly baptised child.🌿", "p710": "the descent of the holy spirit pogorarea sfantului duh jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, 19th century 🌿«the descent of the holy spirit» – pentecost: 31 may🌿 ▫the icon of «the descent of the holy spirit», icon on glass – model: nicula, 19th century ▫“the holy spirit is the living breath of the church; without him, everything is merely a lifeless form.” (saint john chrysostom) ▫«the descent of the holy spirit» is the day on which the holy spirit came down upon the holy apostles, thus founding the christian church. it is a feast of grace, of light and of faith.", "p715": "the holy trinity sfanta treime jesus christ and the great feasts •«the holy trinity» in an icon on glass, a study after an icon made by ioan pop of fagaras in the mid-19th century, known for his unmistakable style, which works within the byzantine tradition, with baroque influences and, of course, local folk art. • the theological approach («the holy trinity»): the attempt to render the common divine essence points to an effort to visualise a theological dogma, not merely to illustrate a biblical scene, which gives the icon a special spiritual depth. • the icon is not available; it was ordered and has already arrived, with joy, in constanta.🤍", "p718": "saint irene the great martyr sfanta mare mucenita irina saints and archangels 🌿«saint irene of magedon, the great martyr» – icon on glass - saint irene is celebrated on 5 may - saint irene of magedon, the great martyr, lived in the 4th century and suffered for her faith in christ. - her name, irene, means \"peace\" in greek. - she is known for preaching christianity despite persecution, and for bringing many people to the faith through her sufferings. - her story is one of faith, courage and perseverance.", "p719": "saint john the baptist sfantul ioan botezatorul saints and archangels • «saint john the baptist» in a small icon on glass ❀ • saint john the baptist was the last of the prophets, the forerunner and baptiser of our lord jesus christ, “the greatest among those born of women” (matthew 11:11)", "p722": "the life-giving spring izvorul tamaduirii the mother of god savu moga, tara fagarasului, 1877 17 april 17 april: «the life-giving spring» ⊹ a feast on bright friday... it is a feast dedicated to the mother of god, recalling the role of the virgin mary in the salvation of mankind. ⊹ a warm feast dedicated to the mother of god, reminding us of good friday, of the tears and pain of the sorrowful mother... then, the mother of god suffered and wept beside the saviour's cross. today, the tears of the mother of god are a healing spring of hope and of healing from illness, wounds and suffering. ⊹ the icon we are showing you today is “the sorrowful mother of god”, painted in our workshop (model: savu moga, tara fagarasului, 1877). - this work is one of the most dramatic in savu moga's whole body of work, thanks to the elegance, grace and expressiveness of the mother of god's face. - everything stands out against a background with a reddish patina. - groups of cherubim whirl among the figures of the holy spirit, god the father and the crucified jesus. - the elongated body of jesus is fluid and graceful above golgotha. - in the left corner there is a cyrillic inscription, a quatrain, very unusual for master moga, which says: “... he who by his word alone / made the heavens and the earth / is nailed upon the cross / a thing unheard of / 1877”.", "p723": "the resurrection of the lord invierea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts after a 19th-century icon, savu moga «the resurrection of the lord jesus» is the greatest feast of christendom. ⊹\"i am the resurrection and the life; whoever believes in me, though he die, yet shall he live. and whoever lives and believes in me shall never die. do you believe this?\" (jesus to martha, in john) ⊹ in honour of the feast, we are showing you today an icon on glass (model: after a 19th-century icon, savu moga) ⊹ about the icon: -the theme, treated in the western manner, shows jesus holding the banner of victory, standing on the clouds. the soldiers who guarded his tomb look up at him. the two myrrh-bearing women complete the picture, together with a praying angel. -the soldiers wear hussar uniforms: red and green tunics with gold braid, blue trousers, red boots and helmets with red crowns, gilded mounts and plumes. the soldier on the left wears a shirt of gilded chain mail and holds a curved sabre above his head. the composition is set within a border. (description: the national museum of the romanian peasant) ⊹ the icon is not available. if you would like an icon on glass on this theme (or any other iconographic theme), contact me and we will settle the details. ⊹ may the feast of the resurrection be blessed with joy in every soul and in every home! christ is risen!", "p726": "the last supper cina cea de taina jesus christ and the great feasts savu moga, arpasu de sus, tara oltului, 1859 • «the last supper» – icon on glass (model: savu moga, arpasu de sus, tara oltului, 1859) • holy thursday is dedicated to the memory of four events in the life of jesus: the washing of the disciples' feet, the last supper, the high-priestly prayer before the passion, where the emphasis falls on love, and the beginning of the passion with the betrayal of the lord jesus christ. • vasile ioana (priest): “jesus's sermon at «the last supper» is a sermon showing that love should guide our lives.”", "p728": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts • «the nativity of the lord jesus christ», a beautiful, delicate small icon (13x18 cm)❤ • “it is christmas every time you let god love others through you... yes, it is christmas every time you smile at your brother and offer him your hand.” (mother teresa)", "p730": "the annunciation buna vestire the mother of god scheii brasovului, 19th century 25 march • 25 march: «the annunciation» – feast icon (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century) • and now, just the icon of «the annunciation» • “who could clearly describe the emotion of the archangel gabriel, sent to announce to mary, an earthly woman living a heavenly life, that she would conceive and give birth to the creator of heaven and earth?” • at its centre, the icon painted on glass shows the scene of the annunciation to the mother of god by the archangel gabriel: that she would give birth, as a man, to the son of god. the iconographic scene is framed by a simple border that separates it from 10 panels with icons of saints and feasts: the virgin mary, the coronation of the virgin, saints john the baptist, nicholas, basil, george, constantine and helen, demetrius, gregory and peter. • the icon is not available; it will gladly be painted again, to order.", "p731": "saint john climacus sfantul ioan scararul saints and archangels • «the sunday of saint john climacus» is a call to spiritual growth. so let us be patient in the struggle with ourselves, let us not give up even when the road is hard, and let us climb step by step, through prayer and humility.🙏 • on this special day, we are showing you «saint john climacus» in an icon on glass, made to order.", "p733": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, 19th century • «jesus with the vine» – icon on glass (12x18 cm), model: nicula, 19th century • this unusual iconographic depiction is believed to be based on one of the eucharistic prayers that the priest says during the holy liturgy, during the cherubic hymn: “for thou art the offerer and the offered, o christ our god…” (teodor danalache)", "p717": "saint ephraim the new sfantul efrem cel nou saints and archangels 5 may • saint «ephraim the new» is celebrated on 5 may • saint «ephraim the new» (1384–1426) is one of the most beloved saints of the orthodox church in modern times, called the “quick helper” and a great wonderworker. he is also known as a great martyr, a wonderworker and a swift healer of illness, especially cancer, depression and addiction. • from the age of 14, saint ephraim the new lived in the monastery of the annunciation near nea makri, where he was also martyred. • the icon was ordered, so it is not available.🙏", "p712": "the burning bush of the mother of god rugul aprins al maicii domnului the mother of god 8 march “the burning bush of the theotokos”, icon painted on glass ▪ this icon is inspired by several depictions, one of them being the first such icon to reach our country, in the 1940s, at the antim monastery in bucharest. many generations of the church's servants and of the faithful have prayed before this icon at the antim monastery, and it also inspired the well-known hesychast movement “the burning bush”, a group that kept the fire of faith alive in the hearts of many romanians during the communist rule. ▪ the icon “the burning bush” shows a large eight-pointed star in the form of overlapping rhombuses, with the mother of god holding the saviour in her arms at their centre. four of the eight points are red, representing the fire, and the other four, painted green, symbolise that the bush did not burn but remained whole. on the points of the red star are the symbols of the four holy evangelists: the angel (saint matthew), the lion (saint mark), the ox (saint luke) and the eagle (saint john), and on the four points of the green star the holy angels are depicted. ▪ the icon is not available. if you would like an icon on this theme, contact us.", "p739": "adam and eve in paradise adam si eva in rai jesus christ and the great feasts second half of the 19th century 22 february ⊹22 february 2026: «the sunday of the expulsion of adam from paradise», also known as «cheesefare sunday» ⊹archimandrite ioanichie balan: “how wonderful is the order of the church! great lent begins with the expulsion of adam and ends with the crucifixion of the lord; it begins with death and ends with the resurrection, begins with tears and ends with joy, begins with punishment and ends with man's reconciliation with god through the holy sacraments.” ⊹«adam and eve»: icon on glass, model from the second half of the 19th century.", "p740": "the annunciation buna vestire the mother of god scheii brasovului, 19th century •«the annunciation» in an icon on glass (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century)🙏 •the annunciation, celebrated on 25 march, marks the moment when the archangel gabriel announced to the virgin mary that she would give birth to jesus christ. this feast symbolises joy, hope and the beginning of salvation; it is a day of \"good news\".🌺 •the icon was ordered, so it is not available. we look forward with joy to a new icon on this theme.❤", "p744": "simeon the righteous dreptul simeon saints and archangels 3 february simeon the righteous – 3 february • simeon the righteous teaches us something essential: “god comes at the right time... and how hard it is for us to wait... we wait for an answer to our prayer... we wait for healing... we wait for a miracle in the family... we wait for something in our life to change... that is why let us not forget: let us lift up our hearts... amen!” (fr. vasile beni) • the icon on glass i am showing you today was ordered (many years ago) for a church that i love.", "p747": "jesus christ surrounded by the holy apostles iisus hristos inconjurat de sfintii apostoli jesus christ and the great feasts workshop in lancram, sebes valley, second half of the 19th century • «jesus christ surrounded by the holy apostles» – icon on glass (model: workshop in lancram, sebes valley, second half of the 19th century) • about the icon: jesus christ is painted in the centre, shown frontally, in a high bust. the image of jesus is set within a border with a “rope motif”. each saint is framed in a medallion: saint john the evangelist and the holy apostles peter, paul, matthew, luke, simon, philip, james, bartholomew, thomas, andrew and mark. • the icon is not available. if you would like an icon on this theme, contact me.", "p749": "saints cyril and nicetas sfintii chiril si nichita saints and archangels • two saints are depicted in this icon painted on glass: saint cyril and saint nicetas – a special gift for two little brothers. • cyril of alexandria was patriarch of alexandria, a prolific writer and the main protagonist of the christological controversies of the 4th and 5th centuries. - he is celebrated both on 9 june and on 18 january, together with saint athanasius of alexandria. • saint nicetas the confessor was born in caesarea of bithynia, in asia minor. as an adult he entered the monastery of saint sergius of medikion, on mount olympus. he was ordained a priest, and in the year 800, after the death of abbot nikephoros, saint nicetas was made abbot. - he is celebrated on 3 april, together with saint illyricus.", "p750": "the mother of god, “the unfading flower” maica domnului „floarea neprihanita” the mother of god 15 january • 15 january: mihai eminescu's day and the day of national culture • together with “rise over me, o gentle light” by the incomparable poet, we celebrate the day of national culture with an icon of the mother of god, “the unfading flower” • the mother of god, eminescu's “gentle light”: “rise over me, o gentle light, once more, as in my heavenly dream of long ago; o holy mother, virgin evermore, come to the night of all my thoughts below. do not let my last hope die away, although my sins are heaped up mountain-high; with your warm gaze, so full of mercy, pray, look down with pity on me from the sky. a stranger to all, lost in the deep pain of my own nothingness and frailty, i can believe no more, my strength is gone. give me my youth, give back my faith again, and from your starry heaven come to me, that i may love you, mary, from now on!”", "p752": "the baptism of the lord botezul domnului jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, first half of the 19th century 6 january ⚜6 january: the baptism of the lord⚜ • “the baptism of christ in the jordan is linked to the revelation of the holy trinity to mankind. there is no greater revelation than this, for through it the triune being of god is shown to us.\" (saint nikolai velimirovic) • on the eve of the great feast, the icon i am showing you today is one of the versions of this theme made in our workshop: “the baptism of the lord\", model: scheii brasovului, first half of the 19th century.", "p756": "the resurrection of the lord invierea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts 19th-century icon, savu moga today we are showing you a second icon, painted almost identical to the previous one (from april): «the resurrection of the lord jesus» (a study after a 19th-century icon, savu moga) this icon was ordered from braila🌺. if you would like an icon on glass on this theme (or any other iconographic theme), contact me and we will settle the details.", "p759": "saint zoe the martyr sfanta mucenita zoe saints and archangels 18 december • 18 december: «saint zoe the martyr» (icon painted on glass) • during the persecution of the christians (under the reign of nero), zoe was caught while praying at the tomb of the holy apostle peter. after five days in prison, she suffered a martyr's death. • “happy name day” to the ladies who bear the name «zoe», a name meaning “life”.🌺", "p761": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels icon from 1887, arpasu de sus, savu moga 6 december ⚜«saint nicholas the hierarch» – 6 december • “saint nicholas was gentle, without malice and humble in spirit, guarding himself against pride. to the poor he was a father; to the needy, merciful; a comforter to those who wept; a helper to the wronged, and a great benefactor to all.” • we welcome the great feast with an icon on glass (a study after an icon from 1887, arpasu de sus, savu moga) • young and old, get your boots ready! saint nicholas is coming soon! • happy name day to all who celebrate!🌼", "p762": "saint andrew the apostle sfantul apostol andrei saints and archangels 30 november ⚜30 november: «saint andrew the apostle» • father cleopa: “... we romanians have a church of apostolic origin, founded in the first century after the ascension of the lord into heaven. saint andrew the apostle brought us to christianity and celebrated the first holy liturgy on romanian soil. he freed us from demons and passions and united us with christ through sacrifice and the liturgy. he taught us how to be saved through humility, through prayer and through love ...” • the icon – my own composition – that i am showing you today is not available; it was ordered as a gift for a friend of ours, one of those celebrating their name day today. • “happy name day” to all our friends who bear the name of saint andrew! 🌺", "p764": "the entry of the mother of god into the temple intrarea in biserica a maicii domnului the mother of god savu moga, 1860 21 november ⚜«the entry of the mother of god into the temple» (21 november) ✧ “today the virgin mary was brought to jerusalem, into the lord's temple, to pray, to speak with god and with the angels, to be deified, to become a living temple of the holy spirit, to prepare to give birth on earth to jesus christ, the saviour of the world\" – from a sermon by father cleopa (21 november 1999). ✧ as we wait to celebrate this great feast (the first of the nativity fast), we are showing you one of the icons on this theme, an icon i painted on glass (model: savu moga, 1860) for a holy church in dobrogea.", "p768": "the holy archangels michael and gabriel sfintii arhangheli mihail si gavriil saints and archangels 8 november «the archangels michael and gabriel» – one of the icons depicting the holy archangels, which we are showing you today, 8 november. - • michael, whose name means “the power of god”, is the commander of the heavenly hosts and the first of the choir of the holy archangels. • gabriel, whose name means “man of god”, is the archangel of good tidings; his mission is to announce to people the great mysteries of god. • both are leaders of the choirs of angels and guides of souls towards paradise. • happy name day to all who celebrate!", "p769": "martyrs and heroes of the romanian people martiri si eroi ai neamului romanesc martyrs and heroes 2 november • today, 2 november 2025, marks 241 years since the outbreak of the peasant uprising led by horea, closca and crisan.", "p770": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts jesus christ – the true vine • this unusual iconographic depiction is believed to be based on one of the eucharistic prayers that the priest says during the holy liturgy, during the cherubic hymn: “for thou art the offerer and the offered, o christ our god…” (teodor danalache, crestinortodox.ro) • this small icon was not ordered, nor is it for sale. i painted it one day because i missed this special theme.", "p772": "saint demetrius the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic dimitrie saints and archangels marginimea sibiului, second half of the 19th century 26 october • 26 october: the feast of the holy great martyr «demetrius the myrrh-streaming» (dumitru), one of the great holy martyrs, a wonderworking and healing saint. • we welcome this great feast with an icon painted on glass in our workshop (model: marginimea sibiului, second half of the 19th century). • happy name day to all who celebrate!🍂", "p775": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise nicula, 19th century ⊹“the table of paradise\" or “the heavenly feast\" in an icon painted on glass (model: nicula, 19th century). a theme i have been asked for many, many times over the years. ⊹ one of the versions i have painted is this one, the most recent, which i am showing you today. the icon has gone, with joy, to braila.🌺", "p777": "the dormition of the mother of god adormirea maicii domnului the mother of god • «the dormition of the mother of god» – a study after a valuable icon from the collection of the vasile grigore art museum (vasile grigore was a painter and collector). it is an icon on glass (tara oltului, 19th century) listed as a national treasure. • the icon i am showing you today (made in our workshop) is not available; it was ordered for a holy church in brasov county.", "p779": "the holy archangels michael and gabriel sfintii arhangheli mihail si gavriil saints and archangels ✤“the holy archangels michael and gabriel, leaders of the choirs of angels and guides of souls towards paradise” in a new icon on glass; this time, the order is for a holy orthodox church in transylvania.", "p780": "the exaltation of the holy cross inaltarea sfintei cruci jesus christ and the great feasts 14 september ✠ 14 september – «the exaltation of the holy cross» • «the exaltation of the holy cross» is the oldest and most important of the christian feasts dedicated to honouring the cross of jesus. • tomorrow's feast is a symbol of christ's victory over death and sin, and stands for hope and salvation for all the faithful. • the icon i am showing you today, [on the day of the great feast of «the exaltation of the holy cross»], depicts «saints constantine and helen», in the traditional model of the two emperors standing on either side of the holy cross.", "p783": "saint alexander the hierarch sfantul ierarh alexandru saints and archangels 30 august ▪ every year on 30 august, orthodox christians celebrate saint alexander, patriarch of constantinople, known as ”the protector of mankind”. ▪“happy name day!” to all named alexandra and alexandru!🌿", "p755": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise workshop in scheii brasovului, 19th century ▫ «the table of paradise» – a personalised icon ▫ the icon «the table of paradise» is divided by diagonal bands into five fields showing: the mother of god with the child, christ pantocrator, saint paraskeva, saint nicholas and, often, a floral element at the centre of the composition, symbolising paradise. ▫ for a personalised icon, on request we replace saint paraskeva and saint nicholas with the saints you prefer. in today's icon, the saints of «the table of paradise» are saint eugenia and saint claudius. ▫ saint claudius the martyr – 19 march ▫ happy name day to all who celebrate!", "p790": "saint irene the great martyr sfanta mare mucenita irina saints and archangels 🌿saint irene of magedon, the great martyr • a new saint, a new icon on glass, a new and unusual gift. the icon of saint irene was ordered by a young husband as a surprise for his wife. • a few words about saint irene, whom some of us have not yet come to know: - saint irene of magedon, the great martyr, lived in the 4th century and suffered for her faith in christ. - her name, irene, means \"peace\" in greek. - she is one of the twelve holy virgin martyrs who appeared to saint seraphim of sarov and to the nun eupraxia. - saint irene learned about christ from apelian and was baptised by saint timothy, the disciple of the holy apostle paul. - saint irene is celebrated on 5 may. - she is known for preaching christianity despite persecution, and for bringing many people to the faith through her sufferings. - her story is one of faith, courage and perseverance.", "p791": "saint elijah the prophet sfantul proroc ilie saints and archangels 20 july • 20 july: the romanian orthodox church celebrates the ascent into heaven of the holy great prophet elijah the tishbite, a saint honoured as a great wonderworker and bringer of rain in times of drought. • the most recent of the icons on glass from our workshop on the theme «the ascent of the holy prophet elijah into heaven, with scenes from his life» was ordered for an adorable little boy. • this work is inspired by an icon from a workshop in scheii brasovului, second half of the 19th century. • happy name day to all who celebrate!🌸", "p792": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels 🌿a new icon on glass: saint paraskeva, “protector of the pure in heart, a spring of faith, patience and comfort for those in distress”. - the small icon will be a special gift. - white frame, with a stand on the back. - glass size: 9 x 14 cm", "p794": "saint charalambos the hieromartyr sfantul sfintit mucenic haralambie saints and archangels 🌼 a new icon of saint charalambos. 🌿 saint charalambos the hieromartyr, protector of the poor and the sick and deliverer from plague, a saint to whom the romanian peasant (especially in 18th–19th century transylvania) once prayed for protection from plague, cholera, typhoid fever and the other epidemics that used to ravage people. the same romanian peasant “painted” saint charalambos in countless icons on glass. one of them is the model for the icon i am showing you today (workshop in scheii brasovului, 19th century) 🎨 about the icon: the icon shows saint charalambos binding the plague, and so saving the city. charalambos is shown in the usual way (standing, dressed in robe, mantle and omophorion, with the holy book and halo, giving a blessing), trampling the plague, which is bound by a chain fastened to his belt. the plague, carrying a scythe, has the face of a horned man. on either side of the saint, in the background, the image is enriched by a cityscape with palaces and fortified walls. the ground is rendered by bands of colour bearing hatching, crosses and flowers. from high in the sky the scene is watched over by jesus, who blesses him, and by an angel holding out a wreath of flowers to him. they are seated on clouds. on the light-blue background are large unoutlined flowers and black stars (source of the description: the national museum of art of romania)", "p795": "saint martin of tours sfantul martin de tours saints and archangels ✨saint martin of tours (a scene from his life) ~ icon painted on glass • saint martin is celebrated on 11 november and on 4 july (the date he was raised to bishop, in 371). • a short biography of an ascetic hierarch: • saint martin is one of the most popular saints in the catholic church, and he is also venerated as a saint in the orthodox church. saint martin was born around the year 316 in savaria (in the province of pannonia, today szombathely in hungary), the son of a pagan roman tribune, but he received a christian education in pavia, his father's home town, becoming a catechumen at the age of ten. obeying his father, he had to enlist in the roman imperial army, serving in the bodyguard of emperor constantius ii. posted to the cavalry legions at amiens (in gaul), he once met a nearly naked beggar at the city gate. moved with pity, he cut his cloak (called “cappa” in latin) in two with his sword and gave half of it to the man in need. the following night he dreamt of the lord christ, who revealed to him that he himself had been present in the form of the poor man. • the icon is not available. it was ordered as a gift for a wonderful person.", "p751": "the mother of god, “the nursing mother” maica domnului „cea care alapteaza” the mother of god 12 january ✤ 12 january: the feast of the icon of the mother of god “the nursing mother” (galaktotrophousa) • “how shall i approach your swaddling clothes, you who are wrapped in rays\"? says the mother of god in a prayer-hymn on the nativity of the lord, written by saint ephrem the syrian. • over time, this icon has been made on wood or on glass, in various versions. one of the oldest such depictions of the mother of god is on the holy mountain of athos (hilandar monastery). other depictions of this theme, as miniatures, are found in manuscripts. many delightful depictions are found in the icons on glass of the transylvanian icon painters. one of them was made in a workshop in scheii brasovului in the second half of the 19th century, and it is the model after which we made this icon in our workshop. • the icon “the nursing mother” (galaktotrophousa) is celebrated on 12 january and 2 july. • the icon is not available; contact me if you would like an icon on this theme.", "p797": "the holy apostles peter and paul sfintii apostoli petru si pavel saints and archangels 18th century 29 june • 29 june: «the holy apostles peter and paul» – in a small icon on glass (13x18 cm), 18th-century model. • “the holy apostles peter and paul are celebrated for their faith, courage and devotion. they became pillars of the church, and their teachings remain essential spiritual landmarks.” • “do not repay evil with evil or insult with insult, but on the contrary, bless, for to this you were called, that you may inherit a blessing. (1 peter 3:9)” 🌿 happy name day to all who celebrate!🌿", "p799": "saint eugenia the martyr sfanta mucenita eugenia saints and archangels 24 december • saint eugenia the martyr – the orthodox church celebrates her on 24 december. • we welcome the feast with an icon painted on glass, ordered from bacau as a joyful gift for a young lady. • happy name day to all the ladies who bear this name!🌺", "p801": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise • «the table of paradise» is an iconographic synthesis that first appears in the 18th-century woodcuts from hasdate. • it was later often painted in the icons on glass from nicula (19th century), where the model of the icon i am showing you today also comes from. • icons on this theme show the mother of god with the child, christ blessing, saint paraskeva and saint nicholas, each set within a rhombus. at the client's request, the saints in the lower rhombuses can be replaced, on request, with the saints you wish.", "p802": "the holy trinity sfanta treime jesus christ and the great feasts workshop in scheii brasovului, 19th century 9 june ✤ 9 june 2025 – the holy trinity ✤ • fr. teofil paraian: \"we believe that god is one in being and threefold in person. it is a mystery of our faith, perhaps the greatest mystery, something we cannot understand but can receive through faith. this is the divine revelation.\" • on the monday after pentecost sunday (which is dedicated to glorifying the holy trinity), we are showing you the icon painted on glass in our workshop: «the holy trinity and the coronation of the mother of god» (model: workshop in scheii brasovului, 19th century) • the scene shows the holy trinity (the spiritual unity of the three divine persons): jesus christ carrying the cross of the crucifixion, god the father with the orb and sceptre (the insignia of the almighty), and the holy spirit (as a white dove framed by the sun) sending down his blessing. the first two hold a crown above the head of the virgin mary (kneeling, dressed in a red maphorion, with her hands crossed on her chest). the figures are ”held up” by clouds. • this icon was made to order, so it is not available. if you would like a similar icon, contact me.", "p803": "the descent of the holy spirit pogorarea sfantului duh jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, 19th century 🌿«the descent of the holy spirit» – pentecost 🌿 ▫ «the descent of the holy spirit», the day on which the holy spirit came down upon the holy apostles, thus founding the christian church. it is a feast of grace, of light and of faith. ▫ the icon of «the descent of the holy spirit» (model: nicula, 19th century) is one of the recent icons painted in the workshop ▫“the holy spirit is the living breath of the church; without him, everything is merely a lifeless form.” (saint john chrysostom)", "p805": "the ascension of the lord inaltarea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, early 19th century 21 may • 21 may – «the ascension of the lord» – icon on glass (model: nicula, early 19th century) • the scene shows «the ascension of christ», the moment when the saviour rises into heaven in glory, while the apostles and the mother of god look on in wonder and faith. • “the ascension of christ in glory and his sitting at the right hand of the father is the image of the complete deification of his humanity. through all his acts – incarnation, death, resurrection – he gradually deified the human nature he had taken on, but through the ascension he transfigured it completely. thanks to the supreme transfiguration of his body, christ can dwell within those who believe in him. the ascension of the lord does not mean his withdrawal from creation, for he continues to be present and at work through the holy spirit. the bodily ascension into heaven is a testimony that man was created for eternity, for the son presents himself to the father not only as god, but also as man.” (fr. florin vanatoru)🙏", "p807": "saints constantine and helen, the emperors sfintii imparati constantin si elena saints and archangels 21 may ✨21 may: «saints constantine and helen, the emperors», models of faith, wisdom and devotion to christianity. • we welcome the great feast of saints constantine and helen with an icon on glass painted in our workshop, inspired by an icon on glass from the nicula workshop, mid-19th century. • happy name day to all named «constantin and elena»! may they protect you and guide you on the path of faith! 🌺🙏🌺", "p808": "adam and eve in paradise adam si eva in rai jesus christ and the great feasts 🌟a new icon painted on glass – «adam and eve in paradise» today i am happy to show you my most recent work: an icon on glass [depicting adam and eve in paradise], made with care and prayer in every detail. 🎨size: [18x24 cm] 🖌technique: painting on glass, egg-emulsion tempera and gold leaf. every brushstroke was made with thoughts of light, faith and the beauty of tradition. i hope this icon brings peace and blessing to the souls of those who look at it. 🙏 with gratitude for every like and share!", "p810": "the holy trinity in a single body sfanta troita a treimii intr-un singur trup jesus christ and the great feasts with emotion, as we wait for the exit-poll results of the 2025 presidential election, i am showing you a new icon painted in our workshop: «the holy trinity in a single body» – a study after a rare icon that i admired at the astra national museum complex in sibiu. its author is believed to be ioan costea, second half of the 19th century. about the icon: the holy trinity in one body is depicted through the image of the saviour jesus christ blessing with his right hand and holding in his left hand the sceptre, the symbol of almighty power. the saviour is shown floating on a chain of clouds. his three-faced countenance is framed by a triangular halo, a symbol of the trinity. on each side, two cherubim keep watch over him. the icon is not available. on a new order, i will gladly paint this special theme again.", "p815": "the resurrection of the lord invierea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts 19th-century icon, savu moga «the resurrection of the lord jesus» (a study after a 19th-century icon, savu moga) ⊹the theme, treated in the western manner, shows jesus holding the banner of victory, standing on the clouds. the soldiers who guarded his tomb look up at him. the two myrrh-bearing women complete the picture, together with a praying angel. the soldiers wear hussar uniforms: red and green tunics with gold braid, blue trousers, red boots and helmets with red crowns, gilded mounts and plumes. the soldier on the left wears a shirt of gilded chain mail and holds a curved sabre above his head. the composition is set within a border. (description: the national museum of the romanian peasant) ⊹the icon is not available. if you would like an icon on glass on this theme (or any other iconographic theme), contact me and we will settle the details. ⊹may the feast of the resurrection be blessed with joy in every soul and in every home!", "p818": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts 1872, arpasu de sus, savu moga «the entry of the lord into jerusalem» – icon on glass • “palm sunday is the bridge from the holy forty days to the week of the holy passion. the lord enters jerusalem in an entry both humble and triumphant... and we, the new and spiritual israel, prepare to welcome the lord, who comes meek and humble to enter the jerusalem of our souls.” (father petroniu tanase) • we welcome the great feast with an icon painted in our workshop, model: 1872, arpasu de sus, savu moga. • the icon is not available; it was ordered by a dear priest from dobrogea. if you like this iconographic theme, contact me to settle the details. • happy palm sunday!🌾", "p819": "jesus christ surrounded by the holy apostles iisus hristos inconjurat de sfintii apostoli jesus christ and the great feasts workshop in lancram, sebes valley, second half of the 19th century «jesus christ surrounded by the holy apostles» – icon on glass, painted in our workshop. model: workshop in lancram, sebes valley, second half of the 19th century. today, the lancram icon that inspired us belongs to the parish of grinties, just 10 km from the border of the former austro-hungarian empire. the church was built in 1793–1794 by transylvanian woodworkers who had already settled in the area. the habsburg empire was forcing romanians to accept the greek catholic rite and to leave the orthodox faith. and so, real communities of transylvanians formed in moldavia, bringing with them their traditions, their dress, their faith and their icons on glass, unique in the world. about the icon: jesus christ is painted in the centre, shown frontally, in a high bust. the image of jesus is set within a border with a “rope motif”. each saint is framed in a medallion: saint john the evangelist and the holy apostles peter, paul, matthew, luke, simon, philip, james, bartholomew, thomas, andrew and mark. the icon is not available. if you would like an icon on this theme, contact me.", "p821": "saint ephraim the new sfantul efrem cel nou saints and archangels «saint ephraim the new, the venerable martyr» – icon on glass • the saint is known as the “quick helper and healer of illness”, and is one of the most beloved saints of recent times. • «saint ephraim the new, the venerable martyr» is celebrated in the orthodox calendar on two main days: - 5 may: the main feast day, marking the day of his martyrdom (5 may 1426). - 3 january: marks the finding of his relics (3 january 1950) and is considered a second day of veneration. • the icon was ordered a few months ago by a wonderful family from mangalia.", "p822": "the annunciation buna vestire the mother of god scheii brasovului, 19th century 25 march the annunciation – 25 march ▫ the annunciation, the day the archangel gabriel met the mother of god. \"who could clearly describe the emotion of the archangel gabriel, sent to announce to mary (an earthly woman living a heavenly life) that she would conceive and give birth to the creator of heaven and earth?\" source: doxologia.ro ▫ the feast icon on glass (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century) shows at its centre the scene of the annunciation to the mother of god by the archangel gabriel: that she would give birth, as a man, to the son of god. the iconographic scene is framed by a simple border that separates it from 10 panels with icons of saints and feasts: the virgin mary, the coronation of the virgin, saints john the baptist, nicholas, basil, george, constantine and helen, demetrius, gregory and peter.", "p824": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god 8 march 8 march – women's day to celebrate «women's day», i have chosen a few words about «the mother of god – woman par excellence” and one of the icons on glass painted in our workshop, depicting «the coronation of the mother of god». his eminence calinic, archbishop of suceava and radauti: “the mother of god was blessed by god with an unimaginable dignity. she is woman par excellence. the being who gives birth to christ is not just any woman, but woman par excellence, blessed by god with an unimaginable dignity. and jesus is not the son of joseph the righteous, but of mary alone, being conceived “of the holy spirit” (matthew 1:20). this link between the virgin conception and the work of redeeming mankind is also captured in the verses saying that “she will bear a son” (matthew 1:21) and that “he will save his people from their sins” (matthew 1:21).” under the protection of the mother of god: happy women's day, ladies!", "p825": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts ▫ “the nativity of christ is the foundation, the beginning of our salvation; without it we would not have gained salvation.” (archimandrite timotheos kilifis)” ▫ «the nativity of the lord» in a beautiful new icon on glass, inspired by the icons made by the incomparable icon painters of 18th-century nicula. ▫ if you would like an icon on this theme, or any other iconographic theme, contact me.", "p828": "saint alexander the hierarch sfantul ierarh alexandru saints and archangels saint alexander the hierarch, patriarch of constantinople every year on 30 august, orthodox christians celebrate saint alexander, known as ”the protector of mankind”. saint alexander is one of the greatest hierarchs of the church and a fearless defender of the christian faith. the icon was made with great joy for a special family from constanta.", "p831": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise nicula, 19th century · a new personalised icon: «the table of paradise» or «the heavenly feast» – icon on glass (model: nicula, 19th century). · the iconographic theme divides the space of the composition into five rhombus-shaped fields, separated by bands decorated with the «rope» motif. · the central rhombus holds an oversized floral motif, which is repeated in the triangular fields next to the five rhombuses. · leaning on the sides of the middle rhombus are the four rhombuses showing the guests taking part in the heavenly feast. the mother of god with the child and jesus christ blessing are always in the upper rhombuses; the others hold other saints, in this case saint basil the great and saint john the baptist. · for a personalised order, you propose the saints you wish to have depicted in the two lower rhombuses.", "p832": "the presentation of the lord intampinarea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, second half of the 18th century 2 february ✨2 february – the presentation of the lord • the presentation of the lord – “a feast of the person who lives in christ” • on this great feast day, every year i show you the same, one and only icon (a naive painting), with the same theme that is rare in romanian iconography, an icon painted in our workshop many years ago (model: nicula, second half of the 18th century). • on 2 february, 40 days after his birth, the saviour's parents performed the ritual of bringing him to the temple to redeem him, as the law of moses required. according to the law, the israelites were required to bring every firstborn male to the temple and dedicate him to the lord, a practice explained by the sparing of the israelites' firstborn on the night they left egypt.", "p835": "saint andrew the apostle sfantul apostol andrei saints and archangels «saint andrew the apostle» – icon on glass this is the second icon on this theme from our workshop. this time, for a lovely family from constanta. so the icon is not available. if you would like an icon on this theme, contact me.", "p836": "the mother of god, “the unfading flower” maica domnului „floarea neprihanita” the mother of god 15 january 15 january – mihai eminescu “choosing you as our queen, we kneel and pray to you: raise us up, and save us from the waves that toss us; be a shield of strength and a wall of salvation, let your adored gaze come down upon us, o most pure mother and ever-virgin, mary! we, who by the saint's mercy cast our shadow on the earth, pray to the compassion of the morning star of the seas; hear our laments, queen above the angels, show yourself from the mists, sweet and clear light, o most pure mother and ever-virgin, mary!” (prayer – mihai eminescu) together with the incomparable poet's “prayer”, we celebrate the day of national culture with an icon of the mother of god called “the unfading flower” or “the lily flower”.", "p838": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels «saint paraskeva» – icon on glass (12x16 cm)", "p839": "the baptism of the lord botezul domnului jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, 19th century 6 january • 6 january: the baptism of the lord (theophany) • \"the baptism of christ in the jordan is linked to the revelation of the holy trinity to mankind. there is no greater revelation than this, for through it the triune being of god is shown to us...\" (saint nikolai velimirovic) • the theme of the baptism of the lord, one of the great events of christendom, also called theophany, epiphany or the divine manifestation, holds an important place in the world of the peasant icons on glass. • the icon on glass (model from scheii brasovului, 19th century) that i am showing you today is one of my early icons, painted almost 6 years ago, when i was entering the fascinating world of icons. this old icon, with its inevitable imperfections, shows jesus christ in a humble attitude, with his hands crossed on his chest, at the moment he is baptised by his forerunner, the great prophet john. • also in a humble attitude is an angel of the lord, holding a towel in both hands as the lord comes out of the waters of the jordan. from the clouds, the holy spirit appears in the form of a dove.", "p843": "the holy transylvanian confessors sfintii marturisitori ardeleni martyrs and heroes 21 october ⚜21 october – the holy transylvanian confessors • hieromonk nicolae mladin said: “they are peaks of holiness resting on the giant shoulders of the faith of the whole church; they are waves of light from the great surge of the waves of faith that filled the troubled centuries of the history of the romanian faithful of transylvania. • raised from the people and bound to the people, bound to the church of their forefathers, in them the will of the whole church found its voice, and the will of all the faithful, the will of the whole people, fought. they are the holy confessors in whom the confession of the church was embodied. they are the representative saints of transylvanian orthodoxy, of the romanian orthodox soul of transylvania.” • the icon with a dedication was painted with joy for a young father from alba iulia.", "p844": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts • “the nativity of the lord, the mystery that gives us (new) birth...” (fr. ioan emilian raza) • on christmas eve, the day before the nativity of the lord, i am showing you an icon on glass inspired by a work from laz, alba, from the last decades of the 19th century. • the icon is not available. contact me if you would like a similar icon. • peace and joy in every home!", "p847": "the ladder of paradise scara raiului jesus christ and the great feasts «the ladder of paradise» – icon on glass, my own composition “we have them all! you and i alike: nine beatitudes, nine holy gospel virtues. this is the gospel of the fast, the gospel of saint john climacus. virtues, brothers, great virtues. the hard struggles of fasting, prayer and humility the lord presented as beatitudes. blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.” (saint justin popovic) the icon was made to order, so it is not available. if you would like a similar icon, contact me to settle the details.", "p849": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels matei timforea, cartisoara, 1894 6 december • 6 december: «saint nicholas the hierarch» •“... saint nicholas... the image of meekness, of zeal for the truth and of compassion for people put into practice...” (father rafail noica) • we welcome the great feast with two of the icons painted in our workshop. each of them depicts «saint nicholas», the great wonderworker. - the first icon: model by matei timforea, cartisoara, 1894 - the second icon: model from arpasu de sus, savu moga, 1887 • happy name day to all who celebrate! in peace! • i vote for europe, not russia!", "p850": "saint andrew the apostle sfantul apostol andrei saints and archangels 30 november ⚜30 november: «saint andrew the apostle» ◘father cleopa: “...we romanians have a church of apostolic origin, founded in the first century after the ascension of the lord into heaven. saint andrew the apostle brought us to christianity and celebrated the first holy liturgy on romanian soil. he freed us from demons and passions and united us with christ through sacrifice and the liturgy. he taught us how to be saved through humility, through prayer and through love...” ◘the icon – my own composition – that i am showing you today is not available; it was ordered as a gift for one of those celebrating their name day today! ◘happy name day to all who bear the name of saint andrew!", "p855": "saint philip the apostle sfantul apostol filip saints and archangels 14 november ✠ 14 november: «saint philip the apostle», celebrated on the first day of the nativity fast. ◘ «saint philip the apostle» was one of the twelve apostles of the lord christ. he also preached the gospel of salvation in the lands of our country, together with saint andrew the apostle. ◘ on the eve of this feast i am showing you an icon painted on glass, ordered as a gift for a little boy from cluj. ◘ happy name day to all who celebrate!", "p721": "saint george the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic gheorghe saints and archangels arpasu de sus, early 19th century 23 april • 23 april – «saint george the great martyr», the victory-bearer, called “the spiritual springtime”. • one of the works painted in our workshop depicting saint george the great martyr is this icon painted on glass, which we are showing you today (model: arpasu de sus, early 19th century) • about the icon: - the scene shows the soldier saint george. born in beirut, he was an army commander under diocletian; he defended the christians and was martyred in 303 ad. he is one of the most venerated saints. - he rides a white horse, dressed in armour and a cloak, with a lance that has a cross at one end, and under the horse we see the dragon pierced by the lance. behind the saint, on the horse's rump, sits the boy leo of amira with a jug in his hand, which he was taking to his master in the field when saint george freed him from slavery to the bulgars. in the distance are the emperor's daughter, saved from the dragon's claws, and the emperor throwing him the keys of the city. • joyful happy name day to all who bear the name of saint george!🥀", "p861": "the holy transylvanian confessors sfintii marturisitori ardeleni martyrs and heroes 21 october ❈ on 21 october, the orthodox church celebrates the holy transylvanian confessors. • over the centuries, the orthodox church of transylvania was a martyr church. countless were the wrongs done by the 18th-century masters of transylvania to the transylvanian church, including its servants and its faithful. but many too were those who fought to defend the orthodox faith of their forefathers against the oppression of the imperial power in vienna. • six holy transylvanian confessors – two priests, two monks and two free peasants, martyrs of the true faith of their forefathers – in an icon painted on glass. saints in whom the whole orthodox church of transylvania is embodied: hierarchs and clergy, monks and hermits, the multitude of the faithful. • these fighters were: oprea miclaus (a peasant from saliste, near sibiu), who suffered death for the true faith; the hieromonks visarion sarai and sofronie of cioara (near orastie); the priests moise macinic of sibiel and ioan of gales (all five celebrated on 21 october); and atanasie todoran of bichigiu, bistrita-nasaud (celebrated on 12 november). • the icon was painted to order, so it is not available. it can be made again, to order.", "p864": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, late 18th century ✨«the nativity of the lord, the mystery that gives us (new) birth». (fr. ioan emilian raza) • as we wait for the great feast of the nativity of the lord, i am showing you one of the icons on glass on this theme (model: nicula, late 18th century) • the icon was ordered from ramnicu valcea, as a gift. • peace and joy in every home!🎄", "p866": "the descent of the holy spirit pogorarea sfantului duh jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, 19th century ▫ for orthodox christians, the feast of pentecost is not just the memory of a historical event. it is a celebration of the faithful's belonging to the church. they have lived the descent of the holy spirit and received “the seal of the gift of the holy spirit” through the sacrament of anointing with holy chrism. ▫“fifty days after the resurrection of the lord, at the jewish feast called pentecost (fifty days after the feast of the exodus), while the apostles and other disciples of the lord jesus christ were gathered together in prayer in the \"upper room\", the holy spirit came down upon them in the form of “divided tongues of fire”, with the sound of a mighty wind, and they began to speak in languages they did not know. at that time there were many pilgrims in jerusalem from the jewish diaspora, come for the feast, who were greatly amazed to hear these unschooled fishermen saying prayers to the lord in the languages of their distant countries.” (this event is described in detail in the acts of the apostles, chapter 2) ▫ the number fifty, from the fifty days after the resurrection, bears witness to eternal and heavenly fullness, being seven times seven, plus one. ▫ the icon of the descent of the holy spirit (model: nicula, 19th century) is especially beautiful, because i painted it on anti-reflective glass.", "p869": "the exaltation of the holy cross inaltarea sfintei cruci jesus christ and the great feasts 14 september every year on 14 september, the orthodox church celebrates «the exaltation of the holy cross» “whenever we go through suffering, trouble or illness, if we make the sign of the holy cross, think of the saviour jesus christ and ask for help, then he, with his merciful love, turns physical suffering into spiritual victory and gives us strength to carry the cross of our life.” (patriarch daniel) the icon i am showing you today, on the day of the great feast of «the exaltation of the holy cross», depicts «saints constantine and helen, the emperors», in the traditional model of the two emperors standing on either side of the holy cross. “... the emperor saw the cross in the sky, and the empress found the cross of christ in the earth. that is why, in the icon of the saints, the cross that joins heaven and earth stands between them. the holy emperors hold the cross between them as the mystery of the boundless love of christ, crucified, risen and ascended in glory. so the holy emperors constantine and helen are bound to the mystery of the holy cross because they felt the power of christ, the power of christ's resurrection hidden mysteriously in his sacrificial, humble and merciful love...” (the patriarch of romania). the icon i am showing you today is not available; a few days ago it arrived in its little home, where it was awaited with the joy of standing beside two other icons painted in our workshop.", "p872": "the coronation of the mother of god incoronarea maicii domnului the mother of god ▪ a small icon with a painted frame (12x17 cm) ▪ a detail from the central scene of «the coronation of the mother of god», from the icon of the same name.", "p830": "saint charalambos the hieromartyr sfantul sfintit mucenic haralambie saints and archangels transylvanian workshop, laz, first half of the 19th century 10 february ⊹10 february: «saint charalambos enthroned, binding the plague» • model: transylvanian workshop, laz, first half of the 19th century • the saint is shown seated on a bishop's throne, symbolising his spiritual power and his victory over death. under the saint's feet or beside the throne there is always a demonic figure, often winged, carrying a scythe. • this scene reflects the popular devotion to the saint who delivered whole communities from devastating epidemics, such as the famous «caragea's plague» in bucharest. • these icons were not only objects of worship; they also had a strong protective (apotropaic) role, guarding the home and the family against contagious diseases. • icons showing saint charalambos in this form are considered collector's pieces. • if you like an icon on this iconographic theme, contact me and we will settle the details.", "p727": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts 1872, arpasu de sus, savu moga ✨«palm sunday – the entry of the lord into jerusalem» – icon on glass • “palm sunday is the bridge from the holy forty days to the week of the holy passion. the lord enters jerusalem in an entry both humble and triumphant... and we, the new and spiritual israel, prepare to welcome the lord, who comes meek and humble to enter the jerusalem of our souls.” (father petroniu tanase) • we welcome the great feast with an icon painted in our workshop (model: 1872, arpasu de sus, savu moga). • the icon is not available; it was ordered by a dear priest from dobrogea. if you like this iconographic theme, contact me to settle the details. • happy name day to all who celebrate!🌾happy palm sunday!🌾", "p883": "saint elijah the prophet sfantul proroc ilie saints and archangels icon from the last quarter of the 19th century, from a transylvanian workshop 20 july saint elijah the tishbite, the prophet – 20 july we welcome the great feast with one of the first icons made in our workshop (2019), ordered for a holy church. the work is a study after an icon from the last quarter of the 19th century, from a transylvanian workshop. today it is in the collection of the national museum of art of romania. happy name day to all who celebrate!🌺", "p856": "saint menas the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic mina saints and archangels scheii brasovului, late 19th century 11 november ❈ «saint menas», protector of the home and of those who have suffered loss, is celebrated by the orthodox church on 11 november. • as we wait for the great feast, i am showing you «saint menas» in an icon painted on glass in our workshop, a study after a rare piece made in a workshop in scheii brasovului at the end of the 19th century. • the icon is not available; it was ordered to bring peace and joy every day to a bright little home in bucharest. if you would like a similar icon, contact me to settle the details.", "p701": "saint paisios the athonite sfantul cuvios paisie aghioritul saints and archangels 12 july • saint «paisios the athonite» (12 july)🌿 • “saint «paisios the athonite» (1924–1994) is a name that brings joy and comfort just by being spoken. after a life of ascetic struggle and of love for god and neighbour, father «paisios the athonite» was officially numbered among the saints, with a day of remembrance (yearly feast) on 12 july.” • the icon of saint paisios that we are showing you today was made in our workshop for a lovely family from maramures.", "p887": "saint martin of tours sfantul martin de tours saints and archangels ✨saint martin of tours ~ icon painted on glass • a short biography of an ascetic hierarch: “saint martin was born around the year 316 in savaria (in the province of pannonia, today szombathely in hungary), the son of a pagan roman tribune, but he received a christian education in pavia (his father's home town), becoming a catechumen at the age of ten. obeying his father, he had to enlist in the roman imperial army, serving in the bodyguard of emperor constantius ii. posted to the cavalry legions at amiens (in gaul), he once met a nearly naked beggar at the city gate. moved with pity, he cut his cloak (called “cappa” in latin) in two with his sword and gave half of it to the man in need. the following night he dreamt of the lord christ, who revealed to him that he himself had been present in the form of the poor man.” (source of the description: doxologia.ro) • saint martin is celebrated on 11 november and on 4 july. • the icon is not available; it was ordered.", "p888": "the mother of god, “the nursing mother” maica domnului „cea care alapteaza” the mother of god 2 july 2 july: the veneration of the icon of the mother of god “the nursing mother” (galaktotrophousa, the nourisher of life) “the mother of god is the true mother of life, our guiding mother and intercessor. she who nourishes all of us who ask for her help in need. unconditionally, at any moment and at any hour of the day or night!” (justinian of maramures and satmar) over time, this icon has been made on wood or on glass, in various versions. one of the oldest such depictions of the mother of god is on the holy mountain of athos (hilandar monastery); other depictions of this theme can be admired in manuscripts and, of course, many delightful depictions are found in the icons on glass of the transylvanian icon painters, one of them (workshop in scheii brasovului, second half of the 19th century) being the model after which we made this icon in our workshop. the icon is not available. if you would like a similar icon, contact me.", "p889": "the holy apostles peter and paul sfintii apostoli petru si pavel saints and archangels 29 june 29 june: «the holy apostles peter and paul» in orthodox iconography (and so also in the icon painted on glass in our workshop, which we are showing you today) the two apostles are painted together: peter holding a bunch of keys and paul a sword. what is the meaning of these two elements, what do these objects signify? fr. constantin sturzu explains: «the keys that saint peter holds are “the keys of the kingdom of heaven”; they unlock the gates of paradise, but only through the sacrament of repentance, or confession. the sword means the diligent preaching of the word of god; so if we receive the word of god, even if it stings at first like a cut from a sword, it then opens the gates of eternity to us, just as a key opens the door of a house.» happy name day to all who celebrate!", "p890": "the holy trinity sfanta treime jesus christ and the great feasts 24 june 24 june 2023: «the holy trinity» • “the holy trinity is the supreme mystery of existence, which explains everything, and without which nothing can be explained.” (father dumitru staniloae) • on the monday after pentecost sunday (which is dedicated to glorifying the holy trinity), we are showing you a few icons painted on glass in our workshop – after different models – whose common theme is «the holy trinity and the coronation of the mother of god». • the scene shows the holy trinity (the spiritual unity of the three divine persons): jesus christ carrying the cross of the crucifixion, god the father with the orb and sceptre (the insignia of the almighty), and the holy spirit (as a white dove framed by the sun) sending down his blessing. the first two hold a crown above the head of the virgin mary (kneeling, with her hands crossed on her chest). the figures are ”held up” by clouds. • these icons were made to order, so they are not available. if you would like an icon on this theme, contact me to settle the details.", "p892": "the holy archangels michael and gabriel sfintii arhangheli mihail si gavriil saints and archangels the holy archangels michael and gabriel – icon on glass • michael, whose name means “the power of god”, is the commander of the heavenly hosts and the first of the choir of the holy archangels. • gabriel, whose name means “man of god”, is the archangel of good tidings; his mission is to announce to people the great mysteries of god. • both are leaders of the choirs of angels and guides of souls towards paradise. • with great joy i worked on a new icon of the two holy archangels; this time it was wanted for a little home in tulcea, where another icon painted in our workshop, the table of paradise, was waiting for it.", "p893": "the ascension of the lord inaltarea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts 13 june 13 june: the ascension of the lord we welcome the great feast with two icons painted in our workshop for a holy church, both inspired by two works made in nicula in the 18th century. “... we cannot think of the lord christ except as the one who sits at the right hand of the father; we cannot consider the lord christ except as the one who is in heaven and everywhere: everywhere with his divinity and in heaven with his human nature...” (father teofil paraian)", "p895": "the little prince micul print other projects “all grown-ups were once children, but few of them remember it...” (the little prince) we remember our childhood looking at the little prince alongside invented characters (the puppy and the cat) in a charming painting on glass, ordered by one of the first people who appreciated, and still appreciate, our icons. happy children's day to children big and small!", "p896": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts a new icon with a special theme, painted in our workshop: the nativity of the lord jesus christ. it is inspired by an icon from 1869 (savu moga, arpasu de sus, which was itself inspired by woodcuts). about the icon: the nativity scene is dominated by jesus on his swaddling cloth, surrounded by the kneeling holy mary, by joseph and by the other figures named in the painters' manuals: the three magi, the shepherds, the two animals – the ox and the horse – and the star that guides the magi and whose rays come down upon the child jesus. at the top, two angels display the text “the nativity of the lord jesus christ”. the icon is not available. if you would like an icon on this theme, contact me.", "p812": "the life-giving spring izvorul tamaduirii the mother of god savu moga, tara fagarasului, 1877 25 april 25 april: «the life-giving spring» ⊹ a feast on bright friday... it is a feast dedicated to the mother of god, recalling the role of the virgin mary in the salvation of mankind. ⊹ a warm feast dedicated to the mother of god, reminding us of good friday, of the tears and pain of the sorrowful mother... then, the mother of god suffered and wept beside the saviour's cross. today, the tears of the mother of god are a healing spring of hope and of healing from illness, wounds and suffering. ⊹ the icon we are showing you today is “the sorrowful mother of god”, painted in our workshop (model: savu moga, tara fagarasului, 1877).", "p902": "the resurrection of the lord invierea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts 19th-century icon, savu moga today we are showing you a new icon painted in our workshop: «the resurrection of the lord jesus» (a study after a 19th-century icon, savu moga) the icon is not available. if you would like an icon on glass on this theme (or any other iconographic theme), contact me and we will settle the details. a serene easter, with joy in every soul and in every home! christ is risen!", "p903": "the lamentation of christ plangerea lui iisus hristos jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, 19th century the lamentation of christ – icon on glass (57x62 cm), a study after an icon from the personal collection of queen marie (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century)", "p904": "the last supper cina cea de taina jesus christ and the great feasts savu moga, arpasu de sus, 19th century «the last supper» – icon on glass (model: savu moga, arpasu de sus, 19th century) \"...with the lord's prayer and blessing, jesus changes the bread and wine into his very body and blood. at this moment, jesus christ establishes the sacrament of holy communion and celebrates the first christian liturgy before his disciples. so the saviour is the first high priest and priest to celebrate the very first liturgy, establishing the sacrament of holy communion... \" (archim. ioanichie balan)", "p905": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts savu moga, arpasu de sus, 1872 “the entry into jerusalem riding on a donkey shows the meekness of the eternal king of the kingdom of heaven. not force, but love will mark the relationships in that kingdom.” (father staniloae) photo: four icons on the same theme, for four recipients, after a single model: savu moga, arpasu de sus, 1872 happy name day to all who celebrate!🌾", "p906": "saint george the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic gheorghe saints and archangels tara oltului, first half of the 19th century 23 april 23 april: «saint george the great martyr, the victory-bearer» we welcome the great feast with an icon painted on glass (model: tara oltului, first half of the 19th century). the icon is not available; a friend of our workshop ordered it as a gift for his wife! «happy name day» to all who celebrate!🌺", "p909": "the coronation of the mother of god incoronarea maicii domnului the mother of god ~icons on glass~ «the coronation of the mother of god», «jesus christ – the true vine» and «the baptism of the lord» are the most recent icons i have painted in our workshop. the first two were shown to you recently, and the third, «the baptism of the lord», i am showing you today. all three, together with the icon «the burning bush», also painted in our workshop, have the joy of lighting up the prayer corner of a special lady who loves icons on glass. photo 1: the icons in the client's home photo 2: «the baptism of the lord jesus christ»", "p913": "the coronation of the mother of god incoronarea maicii domnului the mother of god scheii brasovului, 19th century «the coronation of the mother of god» is an iconographic theme found very often in the wall paintings of orthodox churches, in icons on glass and in the religious paintings of the great western painters of the middle ages. over time, the scene of the coronation of the mother of god has had several versions. in all of them the coronation takes place in heaven. one of the first versions, promoted by western art in the early middle ages, shows the virgin mary enthroned, crowned only by angels. later the iconographic scene was enriched and became more complex. the version we are showing you today is painted on glass after a model from scheii brasovului, 19th century. the icon shows the scene of the coronation of the virgin mary. jesus christ and god the father sit on suggested thrones and hold the mitre they place on mary's head. in the upper register the holy spirit appears as a white dove framed by the sun, flanked on each side by two cherubim floating on clouds. in the lower register, in the middle, mary kneels, dressed in a red maphorion with a halo on her head and her hands crossed on her chest, with cherubim at her feet. all the figures are held up by clouds. the icon is not available; it has gone to constanta together with «the eucharistic jesus» and «the baptism of the lord».", "p916": "the eucharistic christ hristos euharistic jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, early 19th century «the eucharistic christ» – icon on glass (model: scheii brasovului, early 19th century) “the power and essence of the sacrament of the eucharist in the orthodox church lie in the fact that, in the form of the bread and wine consecrated at the holy liturgy, the body and blood of jesus christ are truly given to us. this sacramental realism is felt and lived by every orthodox believer who approaches holy communion, and it is hard to put into words and even harder to render in any iconographic image. yet the romanian peasant, forced by circumstances, managed to create an icon unique in the world, of theological composition, with a deep and original message, which defends eucharistic realism without any ambiguity. this is the icon known as «jesus christ – the true vine», but which should more correctly be called «the eucharistic christ», because it is not about the metaphor of the vine but about the eucharist, in which the body and blood of christ are truly present. the context in which this icon appeared is not known from historical documents, but it can easily be deduced from the troubled history of transylvania. more precisely, the icon was born when, from the 16th century on, calvinist proselytism appeared in transylvania, disputing any sacramental realism and claiming that the holy sacraments had only a symbolic value.“ (rev. assoc. prof. dr. irimie marga)", "p921": "the little prince micul print other projects “the little prince” – an unusual order for a work on glass. do you like this black-and-white rendering? or would you like it better painted in colour?", "p922": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise ❈ the table of paradise – a personalised icon «the table of paradise» was often painted in the icons on glass from nicula (19th century), where the model of the icon we are showing you today also comes from. icons on this theme usually show the mother of god with the child, christ blessing, saint paraskeva and saint nicholas, each set within a rhombus. saint paraskeva and/or saint nicholas can be replaced (on request) by other saints, for a personalised icon. in the lower rhombus of the icon where saint nicholas used to be, this time saint john the baptist is depicted, at the request of the client, who wanted a personalised icon. if you would like to have (or to give) an icon on this theme (personalised or not), contact me to settle the details.", "p925": "saint philip the apostle sfantul apostol filip saints and archangels ✠saint philip the apostle – icon on glass “the value of so many documents speaking of saint philip's mission in scythia assures us that we need no longer hesitate to say: saint philip is the second apostle who sanctified romanian soil by preaching the word of the gospel of christ the saviour.” (prof. emilian popescu) so saint philip the apostle was one of the twelve apostles of the lord christ. he also preached the gospel of salvation in the lands of our country, together with saint andrew the apostle. the icon i am showing you today was ordered as a gift for an adorable child.", "p929": "the presentation of the lord intampinarea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, second half of the 18th century 2 february ✨2 february: the presentation of the lord in the temple on this great feast day i am showing you an icon with a theme that is rare in romanian iconography on glass (model: nicula, second half of the 18th century), an icon that has joined an impressive collection of icons on glass belonging to a lovely romanian family from transylvania. forty days after his birth, the saviour's parents performed the ritual of bringing him to the temple to redeem him, as the law of moses required. according to the law, the israelites were required to bring every firstborn male to the temple and dedicate him to the lord, a practice explained by the sparing of the israelites' firstborn on the night they left egypt. the offering was a lamb and a dove. the poor, who had no lamb, could bring two young pigeons (one of which symbolised the offering of thanks to god for the gift received, while the other was the price of redemption for the child, who would otherwise have had to dedicate his life to the service of god).", "p931": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god ⚜the mother of god “the unfading flower”, icon on glass this icon is also called “the immaculate flower” or “the lily flower”. the lily symbolises the unfading flower of the virginity and purity of the all-pure virgin mary, to whom the church sings in its hymns: “you are the root of virginity and the unwithering flower of purity” (doxologia.ro) the icon is not available; it was ordered as a gift.", "p932": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise", "p934": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god 12 january 12 january: the veneration of the icon «the mother of god, the nursing mother» (galaktotrophousa, the nourisher of life) one of the oldest such depictions of the mother of god is on the holy mountain of athos (hilandar monastery); other depictions of this theme (as miniatures) can be admired in manuscripts and, of course, many delightful depictions are found in the icons on glass of the transylvanian masters, one of them (workshop in scheii brasovului, second half of the 19th century) being the model after which we made this icon in our workshop. the icon is not available; contact me if you would like a depiction on glass of this special theme.", "p936": "the baptism of the lord botezul domnului jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, 19th century 6 january 6 january: the baptism of the lord (theophany) the theme of the baptism of the lord, one of the great events of christendom, also called theophany, epiphany or the divine manifestation, holds an important place in the world of the peasant icons on glass. two similar versions of the same theme painted in our workshop (model from scheii brasovului, 19th century) show jesus christ in a humble attitude, with his hands crossed on his chest, at the moment he is baptised by his forerunner, the great prophet john. also in a humble attitude is an angel of the lord, holding a towel in both hands as the lord comes out of the waters of the jordan. from the clouds, the holy spirit appears in the form of a dove. both icons were ordered, so they are not available.", "p937": "saint nikephoros the leper sfantul nichifor leprosul saints and archangels 4 january ✤ 4 january – «saint nikephoros the leper», a healing and wonderworking saint. • we welcome the feast of saint nikephoros the leper with an icon on glass ordered for a holy church in dobrogea. • the icon shows saint nikephoros with scenes from his life; he is a healing saint who became especially popular during the covid-19 pandemic. • “he suffered from leprosy and was patient, merciful and humble, and god gave him the gift of healing the sick.” (patriarch daniel)", "p938": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god arpasu de sus, 1877 dear friends, today (the day our workshop turns two) i am showing you one of the first icons i painted (2019): «the sorrowful mother of god» (model: arpasu de sus, 1877). it is also my first icon ordered for a holy church. in these two years i began receiving orders from you very soon after the workshop opened, and the orders have continued over these years, so that i have had to schedule them for later periods, and the scheduling continues. thank you for all the icons i have painted in these two years. thank you for your patience and understanding in agreeing to wait your turn. thank you for sharing, commenting on and liking my posts, and so supporting our page, which would not exist without you. i wish you and your families a new year of achievements, health, peace and joy, and for our workshop, many more beautiful icons painted on glass. happy new year!", "p939": "the holy trinity sfanta treime jesus christ and the great feasts workshop in scheii brasovului, 19th century • the icon painted on glass «the holy trinity and the coronation of the mother of god» (model: workshop in scheii brasovului, 19th century) has gone to oradea, to decorate (together with other icons painted earlier in our workshop) the white walls of a romantic little house • if you would like an icon on this theme, contact me to settle the details", "p940": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts icon from nicula, 19th century ✨christmas✨ • on christmas eve i am showing you one of our icons on this theme (a study after an icon from nicula, 19th century) • it may not be the most beautiful icon painted in our workshop, but it is blessed, for it is in a holy place: the cell where my gentle spiritual father, the great scholar father ioanichie balan, lived (sihastria monastery) • photo from the cell: archim. petru balan, december 2023. with thanks! • peace and joy in every home!", "p944": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise «the table of paradise» – icon painted on glass ◘ one more icon on this theme (which i am showing you today) has this time gone to tulcea. it is made in the classic version, with saint paraskeva and saint nicholas in the lower rhombuses of the composition", "p951": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, early 19th century ❈ «jesus with the vine» – icon on glass (model: scheii brasovului, early 19th century) • the theme of this icon is found in the transylvanian peasant icons evoking the mystery of holy communion; • the icon illustrates the parable of the vine: “i am the vine, you are the branches”; • jesus presented himself as the true vine, his father as the vinedresser who planted the true vine, and his disciples as the true branches of this vine. it is an archetype according to which the essential elements of life – for food, healing and worship – grew out of the primordial sacrifice; • the icon is not available; if you like this extraordinary theme, contact me and we will settle the details of the order", "p952": "saint menas the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic mina saints and archangels 11 november ❈ «saint menas» (protector of the home and of those who have suffered loss) is celebrated by the orthodox church on 11 november • today i am showing you an icon on glass of «saint menas», a rare piece made in a workshop in scheii brasovului at the end of the 19th century • this icon has not yet been made in our workshop; i would be especially glad to receive orders for this theme too", "p860": "saint demetrius the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic dimitrie saints and archangels marginimea sibiului, second half of the 19th century 26 october • “share out your earthly wealth... let us seek the heavenly one.” (saint demetrius) • 26 october: the feast of the holy great martyr demetrius the myrrh-streaming (dumitru), one of the great holy martyrs, a wonderworking and healing saint. • we welcome this great feast with an icon on glass painted in our workshop (model: marginimea sibiului, second half of the 19th century) • happy name day to all who celebrate!🍂", "p958": "saint zoe the martyr sfanta mucenita zoe saints and archangels 18 december ❀18 december: «saint zoe the martyr» (icon painted on glass) during the persecution of the christians, zoe was caught while praying at the tomb of the holy apostle peter. after five days in prison, she suffered a martyr's death. “happy name day” to the ladies who bear the name «zoe», a name meaning “life”.", "p959": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels 14 october • 14 october: saint paraskeva... a saint always close to the hearts of christians... as a gentle comforter and a quick helper... • we welcome the feast of saint paraskeva by showing you the most recent of the icons on this theme painted in our workshop • happy name day to all who celebrate!", "p962": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise ✧ the table of paradise – a personalised icon • «the table of paradise» is an iconographic synthesis that first appears in the 18th-century woodcuts from hasdate • it was later often painted in the icons on glass from nicula, where the model of the icon we are showing you today also comes from (19th century) • icons on this theme show the mother of god with the child, christ blessing, saint paraskeva and saint nicholas, each set within a rhombus • this time, the lower rhombuses of the icon hold saint anne and saint constantine, at the request of the client, who wanted a personalised icon • if you would like to have (or to give) an icon on this theme (personalised or not), contact me to settle the details", "p964": "saint demetrius the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic dimitrie saints and archangels marginimea sibiului, second half of the 19th century ✧ saint demetrius the great martyr, the myrrh-streaming (or saint dumitru), in an icon (42 x 30 cm) painted on glass – model: marginimea sibiului, second half of the 19th century ✧ the icon was painted to order, so it is not available ✧ would you like an icon on this theme? contact me and we will settle the details", "p870": "the nativity of the mother of god nasterea maicii domnului the mother of god nicula, early 19th century 8 september the akathist of the nativity of the mother of god: “today the door of life is opened, today the ray of the spiritual sun rises, today the mother of joy is born for the salvation of the whole world. be glad, you peoples, and rejoice, and with faith praise her from your hearts thus: rejoice, divine child mary, who today was born for the joy and salvation of the whole world!” the icon on this theme (model: nicula, early 19th century) that we are showing you today was painted for a holy and beautiful orthodox church in dobrogea. about the icon (national institute of heritage): \"lying on a bed above which hangs a rich curtain, saint anne has the baby girl at her feet. joachim urges her to eat from the dishes he brings. a border with the rope motif surrounds the composition. the novelty of the image lies in the way the floor is drawn, like a roof of curved tiles, which focuses all attention on joachim's gesture.\" ❀«happy name day!» to all of you who bear the name of the holy virgin mary.", "p968": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god 4 september ❈ the icon «the mother of god – the burning bush» is celebrated on 4 september • in honour of this feast we are showing you this special theme (the mother of god – the burning bush) in the four icons we have made so far in our workshop", "p971": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts • two icons on glass, both honouring one and the same event: the nativity of our lord jesus christ • the first has gone to arad, a special gift for a special lady • the second was painted for a holy church, alongside several other icons painted in our workshop", "p876": "the holy brancoveanu martyrs sfintii martiri brancoveni martyrs and heroes 16 august «the holy brancoveanu martyrs, the princes who overcame the empire and gained the kingdom» (ioan alexandru) on 16 august, romanian orthodoxy honours the sacrifice of the holy brancoveanu martyrs: prince constantin with his four sons, constantin, stefan, radu and matei, and the counsellor ianache. the icon on glass i am showing you today is one of the versions of this theme made in our workshop, to order.", "p982": "the burning bush of the mother of god rugul aprins al maicii domnului the mother of god 4 september ❈ the icon «the mother of god – the burning bush» is celebrated on 4 september • the icon “the burning bush” shows a large eight-pointed star in the form of overlapping rhombuses, with the mother of god holding the saviour in her arms at their centre. four of the eight points are red, representing the fire, and the other four, coloured green, symbolise that the bush did not burn but remained whole. on the points of the red star are the symbols of the four holy evangelists: the angel (saint matthew), the lion (saint mark), the ox (saint luke) and the eagle (saint john), and on the four points of the green star the holy angels are depicted. • if you would like an icon on this theme, contact me and we will settle the details. the icon i am showing you today is not available.", "p987": "the holy apostles peter and paul sfintii apostoli petru si pavel saints and archangels 29 june • 29 june: «the holy apostles peter and paul» – teachers of faith, repentance and the church's mission in the world • happy name day to all who celebrate! • in orthodox iconography (and so also in the icon painted on glass in our workshop, which we are showing you today) the two apostles are painted together: peter holding a bunch of keys and paul a sword. what is the meaning of these two elements, what do these objects signify? • fr. constantin sturzu explains: «the keys that saint peter holds are “the keys of the kingdom of heaven”; they unlock the gates of paradise, but only through the sacrament of repentance, or confession. the sword means the diligent preaching of the word of god: “for the word of god is living and active, sharper than any two-edged sword, piercing to the division of soul and spirit, of joints and marrow, and discerning the thoughts and intentions of the heart\" (hebrews 4:12). so if we receive the word of god, even if it stings at first like a cut from a sword, it then opens the gates of eternity to us, just as a key opens the door of a house»", "p989": "saints george and demetrius, the great martyrs sfintii mari mucenici gheorghe si dimitrie saints and archangels • «saints george and demetrius, the great martyrs» •the theme, inspired by church painting and the lives of the saints, shows saints george and demetrius, also known as \"the soldier saints\". • in a special composition, the two saints come towards each other and embrace, each bringing his own victory in christ.", "p947": "saint andrew the apostle sfantul apostol andrei saints and archangels 30 november ⚜ 30 november: «saint andrew the apostle» ◘ father cleopa: “saint andrew the apostle brought us to christianity and celebrated the first holy liturgy on romanian soil. he freed us from demons and passions and united us with christ through sacrifice and the liturgy. he taught us how to be saved through humility, through prayer and through love...” ◘ the icon we are showing you today (painted on glass, 22x26 cm) was ordered as a gift for a special person celebrating their name day today! ◘ “happy name day, with faith and love” to the friends of this page who bear the name of saint andrew!", "p992": "the holy trinity sfanta treime jesus christ and the great feasts workshop in scheii brasovului, 19th century 5 june ✤ 5 june 2023 – the holy trinity ✤ • fr. teofil paraian: \"we believe that god is one in being and threefold in person. it is a mystery of our faith, perhaps the greatest mystery, something we cannot understand but can receive through faith. this is the divine revelation.\" • on the monday after pentecost sunday (which is dedicated to glorifying the holy trinity), we are showing you the icon painted on glass in our workshop: «the holy trinity and the coronation of the mother of god» (model: workshop in scheii brasovului, 19th century) • the scene shows the holy trinity (the spiritual unity of the three divine persons): jesus christ carrying the cross of the crucifixion, god the father with the orb and sceptre (the insignia of the almighty), and the holy spirit (as a white dove framed by the sun) sending down his blessing. the first two hold a crown above the head of the virgin mary (kneeling, dressed in a white maphorion, with her hands crossed on her chest). the figures are ”held up” by clouds • this icon was made to order, so it is not available. if you would like a similar icon, contact me", "p816": "the lamentation of christ plangerea lui iisus hristos jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, 19th century ⊹ good friday, silence and prayer... ⊹ “let us kneel with great faith at the tomb of the lord, let us pray and ask forgiveness, let us be reconciled with one another, and on the holy night of easter let us await the mysterious moment of the resurrection of the lord and of our own resurrection” (father cleopa) ⊹ on good friday we are showing you an icon on glass, «the lamentation of christ» – model: scheii brasovului, 19th century. ⊹ about the icon: • the theme of this icon is «the lamentation of jesus», after the descent from the cross and before the burial itself. • the icon is one of the rare compositions developed horizontally, as is proper to the epitaphios. • its central scene shows the laying of jesus christ in the tomb: two apostles hold the shroud at his head and feet, and two angels lift him from the front. in the background, mary is surrounded by the holy women and by archangels; seraphim float in the air and (above the cross) the \"thrones\", angels set in medallions. in the corners of the scene the four evangelists are shown in medallions. in the upper register, between the medallions and the arch of the vault, two landscapes can be seen: mount golgotha on the right and the city of jerusalem on the left. ⊹ the technique is the traditional one: egg tempera and gold leaf. ⊹ the icon is in the collection of a lovely family from brasov, so it is not available. if you would like an icon on this theme or any other iconographic theme, contact me and we will settle the details.", "p1000": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, early 19th century • «jesus with the vine» – icon on glass (model: scheii brasovului, early 19th century) • this icon is also called “the icon of the eucharist”, a theme found only in romanian iconography, especially in transylvania • the iconographic scene shows the risen jesus christ before the cross (standing on the holy table of the altar); from his side grows a vine full of grapes, which christ's hand presses straight into the holy chalice; from the image one can easily deduce that the icon does not aim to highlight the metaphor of the vine (frequent in the new testament writings); it aims to highlight what we find in the holy chalice, namely: \"in the form of the wine flowing from the grapes is the very blood of christ, for the vine grows and is nourished from his side, and on the holy table of the altar lies the very body of the risen christ\" • would you like a similar icon? (this one is not available) contact me and we will settle the details", "p1001": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise nicula, 19th century ◘ «the table of paradise» or «the heavenly feast» – icon on glass (model: nicula, 19th century) ◘ the iconographic theme divides the space of the composition into five rhombus-shaped fields, separated by bands decorated with the «rope» motif ◘ the central rhombus holds an oversized floral motif, which is repeated in the triangular fields next to the five rhombuses ◘ leaning on the sides of the middle rhombus are the four rhombuses showing the guests taking part in the heavenly feast. the mother of god with the child and jesus christ blessing are always in the upper rhombuses; the others hold other saints, in this case saint paraskeva and saint nicholas the hierarch ◘ this icon is not available. for a personalised order, you propose the saints you wish to have depicted in the two lower rhombuses", "p1002": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god arpasu de sus, fagaras ◘ “woman must be cherished, first of all because a woman represents us in the kingdom of heaven: the mother of god” (father arsenie papacioc) ◘ on this sunday (which the church dedicates especially to honouring christian women) we celebrate the myrrh-bearing women, who were the first witnesses of the resurrection of the lord ◘ the icon i am showing you on this special day was painted in our workshop for a holy church (model: arpasu de sus, fagaras)", "p1010": "the holy brancoveanu martyrs sfintii martiri brancoveni martyrs and heroes · the holy brancoveanu martyrs: “the princes who overcame the empire and gained the kingdom“ · the icon on glass (22x26 cm) was painted to order, so it is not available · would you like an icon on glass on this iconographic theme? contact me to settle the details", "p1012": "the mother of god with the child maica domnului cu pruncul the mother of god", "p1013": "the annunciation buna vestire the mother of god scheii brasovului, 19th century 25 march ✤ 25 march – the annunciation ✤ ⁙ on a delightful day when all of nature, in an explosion of colour, awaits the annunciation, we welcome the great feast with a feast icon (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century) ⁙ the icon painted on glass (37x50 cm) shows (in the centre) the scene of the annunciation to the mother of god by the archangel gabriel: that she would give birth, as a man, to the son of god ⁙ the iconographic scene is framed by a simple border that separates it from 10 other iconographic scenes with saints and feasts: the virgin mary, the coronation of the virgin, saints john the baptist, nicholas, basil, george, constantine and helen, demetrius, gregory and peter ⁙ the icon is not available; it will be painted again, to order", "p1016": "saint cyril the hierarch sfantul ierarh chiril saints and archangels 18 march ✝ saint cyril the hierarch, archbishop of jerusalem – 18 march • “god's part is to give grace, and yours is to receive it and keep it” (saint cyril of jerusalem) • the icon on glass i am showing you today (saint cyril and saint nicetas) was ordered for two little brothers • our father among the saints cyril of jerusalem (315–386) was a remarkable theologian and archbishop of jerusalem in the early period of the church. he is one of the holy fathers of the orthodox church of the 4th century who managed to keep the true faith despite all the hard trials. god worked great miracles through saint cyril. he is celebrated in the orthodox church on 18 march • saint nicetas the confessor is celebrated on 3 april", "p1019": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels matei timforea, cartisoara, 1894 ◘ saint nicholas – icon painted on glass (model by matei timforea, cartisoara, 1894) ◘ the icon is made in the traditional technique (egg-emulsion tempera and gold leaf; stained fir frame) ◘ would you like an icon on this beautiful theme? contact me to book your turn", "p1021": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god transylvanian workshop, marginimea sibiului, mid-19th century • “the mother of god, the perfect model of womanhood” (fr. ioan emilian raza) • «the coronation of the mother of god» is the theme of the icon i am showing you at this time when we celebrate woman • the icon is painted on glass in our workshop (model: transylvanian workshop, marginimea sibiului, mid-19th century) • the icon is in a private collection, so it is not available. if you would like an icon on this special theme, contact me and we will settle the details", "p858": "the holy archangels michael and gabriel sfintii arhangheli mihail si gavriil saints and archangels icon painted on glass by savu moga, arpasu de sus, 1890 8 november • 8 november is the day the church dedicates to all the angels who did not turn away from god, which is why this feast appears in the calendar as “the synaxis of the holy archangels michael and gabriel and of all the heavenly powers”. • as we wait for the great feast, i am showing you “the holy archangels michael and gabriel” in two icons on glass painted in our workshop. the first is a study after an icon painted on wood by toma zugravul of barbatesti, valcea, in 1895, an icon kept in a holy church that is a historic monument. the second is a study after an icon painted on glass by savu moga, arpasu de sus, 1890. • this feast dates from the 5th century, beginning as the simple anniversary of the consecration of the church of saint michael the archangel built at the baths of arcadius in constantinople. over time, the feast came to be dedicated to all the holy angels. the seven angels we celebrate are: • michael – translated as “the power of god”. he is the commander of the heavenly hosts and the first of the holy archangels; he carries the fiery sword, and his role is to guard the law of god and to overcome all who do not obey it. he is also the one who stopped the angels from falling from heaven, who defended the body of moses and who brought the ten plagues upon pharaoh's people. it is said that at the end of the age he will raise the dead and gather all nations to judgement. • gabriel is translated as “man of god”, being the archangel of the annunciation. he carries no fiery sword, but the lily of undefiled joy. he was the first to speak the name of jesus, the one who brought the great mystery of the lord's incarnation, the news of the conception, and who gave saint john the baptist his name. • raphael is the healer of human infirmities • uriel is the enlightener of those in darkness • selaphiel is the one who prays for mankind • jegudiel is the glorifier of god and the strengthener of those who do good works • barachiel is the bringer of god's blessing upon the earth • happy name day to all who celebrate!", "p1027": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise • “the table of paradise“: one of the first iconographic themes i discovered almost four years ago, when i stepped with wonder and joy into a new world... a world of icons painted on glass • today i am showing you one of the first versions (of this theme) that i painted in our workshop (photo: in the clients' home)", "p1033": "saint martin of tours sfantul martin de tours saints and archangels ✨saint martin of tours (a scene from his life) ~ icon painted on glass • a short biography of an ascetic hierarch: “ saint martin was born around the year 316 in savaria (in the province of pannonia, today szombathely in hungary), the son of a pagan roman tribune, but he received a christian education in pavia (his father's home town), becoming a catechumen at the age of ten. obeying his father, he had to enlist in the roman imperial army, serving in the bodyguard of emperor constantius ii. posted to the cavalry legions at amiens (in gaul), he once met a nearly naked beggar at the city gate. moved with pity, he cut his cloak (called “cappa” in latin) in two with his sword and gave half of it to the man in need. the following night he dreamt of the lord christ, who revealed to him that he himself had been present in the form of the poor man.” (source of the description: doxologia.ro) • saint martin is celebrated on 11 november and on 4 july • the icon is not available. it was ordered as a gift for a wonderful person", "p842": "saint nektarios the hierarch sfantul ierarh nectarie saints and archangels 9 november dear friends, three years ago we launched this page, dedicated to the icons on glass painted in our workshop. the first icon we showed you that day was the icon of saint nektarios, made for a holy church in macin. today, three years later, we are showing you another icon of saint nektarios, also made for a church. this time, from arad. thank you for all the orders we have received. thank you also for your support, for liking our posts, and for your comments and for sharing the posts with your friends and in groups. today, on our third anniversary, we wish you and your families a new year of achievements, health, peace and joy, and for our workshop, many more beautiful icons painted on glass. happy new year 2025!", "p1038": "the presentation of the lord intampinarea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, second half of the 18th century 2 february ✨2 february – the presentation of the lord✨ • “where is god? wherever he is let in...” (father nicolae steinhardt) • on this great feast day i am showing you an icon with a theme that is rare in romanian iconography (the scene of the presentation of the lord in the temple), an icon painted in our workshop three years ago (model: nicula, second half of the 18th century) • on 2 february (40 days after his birth), the saviour's parents performed the ritual of bringing him to the temple to redeem him, as the law of moses required. according to the law, the israelites were required to bring every firstborn male to the temple and dedicate him to the lord, a practice explained by the sparing of the israelites' firstborn on the night they left egypt • the icon is honoured and sanctified by the very sacred place where it stands, thanks to a lovely romanian family", "p1044": "the mother of god, “the nursing mother” maica domnului „cea care alapteaza” the mother of god workshop in scheii brasovului, second half of the 19th century 2 july ◘ the icon of the mother of god “the nursing mother” (galaktotrophousa) is celebrated twice a year: 2 july and 12 january ◘ over time, this icon has been made on wood or on glass, in various versions. one of the oldest such depictions of the mother of god is on the holy mountain of athos (hilandar monastery); other depictions of this theme (as miniatures) can be admired in manuscripts and (of course) many delightful depictions are found in the icons on glass of the transylvanian icon painters, one of them (workshop in scheii brasovului, second half of the 19th century) being the model after which we made this icon in our workshop ◘ the icon is not available; contact me if you would like an icon on this theme", "p1046": "the baptism of the lord botezul domnului jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, first half of the 19th century 6 january ⚜6 january: the baptism of the lord⚜ ◙ \"...the baptism of christ in the jordan is linked to the revelation of the holy trinity to mankind. there is no greater revelation than this, for through it the triune being of god is shown to us...\" (saint nikolai velimirovic) ◙ the icon i am showing you today (on the eve of the great feast) is the most recent version of the theme “the baptism of the lord\" (model: scheii brasovului, first half of the 19th century) ◙ glass size: 22x26 cm; stained fir frame", "p782": "the burning bush of the mother of god rugul aprins al maicii domnului the mother of god 4 september ⚜ on 4 september the icon of the mother of god “the burning bush” is celebrated • « the mother of god and the “burning bush” » – icon painted on glass, modelled on several depictions, one of them being the first icon on this theme to reach our country, at the venerable foundation of saint antim the iberian, the antim monastery in bucharest, in the 1940s. • many generations of the church's servants and of the faithful have prayed before this icon, and it also inspired the well-known hesychast movement “the burning bush”, a group that kept the fire of faith alive in the hearts of many romanians, especially during the communist rule. • according to the painters' manual, the icon “the burning bush” shows a large eight-pointed star in the form of overlapping rhombuses, with the mother of god holding the saviour in her arms at their centre. four of the eight points are red, representing the fire, and the other four, coloured green, symbolise that the bush did not burn but remained whole. • on the points of the red star are the symbols of the four holy evangelists: the angel (saint matthew), the lion (saint mark), the ox (saint luke) and the eagle (saint john), and on the four points of the green star the holy angels are depicted. • if you would like a similar icon, contact me and we will settle the details. this icon is not available; it was made to order. • this icon is one of the five i have painted in our workshop. i chose the one i am showing you today at random.", "p1048": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, late 18th century ✨« ... the nativity of the lord: the mystery that gives us (new) birth ... » (fr. ioan emilian raza) • as we wait for the great feast of the nativity of the lord, i am showing you one of the icons (painted in our workshop) on this theme (model: nicula, late 18th century) • peace and joy in every home!", "p1051": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels laz, sebes valley, first half of the 19th century 6 december ⚜ « saint nicholas the hierarch » (6 december)⚜ ◘ father rafail noica: “... saint nicholas... the image of meekness, of zeal for the truth and of compassion for people put into practice...” ◘ today i am showing you one of the icons (painted in our workshop) depicting « saint nicholas », the great wonderworker (model: laz, sebes valley, first half of the 19th century) ◘ happy name day to all who celebrate!🥀", "p1052": "saint andrew the apostle sfantul apostol andrei saints and archangels ♦ and so, on the eve of the great feast of \"saint andrew the apostle\", we are showing you an icon (with a very beautiful theme) painted in our workshop: « the coronation of the mother of god » (photo: in the clients' home, 2022) ♦ \"happy name day\" to andreea, andrei and all who celebrate!", "p1054": "the entry of the mother of god into the temple intrarea in biserica a maicii domnului the mother of god savu moga, 1860 21 november ✧21 november: «the entry of the mother of god into the temple» ✧“today the virgin mary was brought to jerusalem, into the lord's temple, to pray, to speak with god and with the angels, to be deified, to become a living temple of the holy spirit, to prepare to give birth on earth to jesus christ, the saviour of the world. amen.\" (fr. cleopa ilie) ✧ as we wait to celebrate this great feast, the first of the nativity fast, i am showing you an icon on this theme that i painted on glass for a holy church in dobrogea. (model: savu moga, 1860)", "p1055": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts laz, last decades of the 19th century “... and christ was born at night, at midnight, and in a cave, to show that he came to bring light and to scatter the darkness... ” father cleopa ◙ the nativity of the lord – icon on glass (29x42 cm), model: laz, last decades of the 19th century ◙ the icon was made to order, so it is not available, but i will gladly paint it again for a future order", "p1056": "saint nektarios the hierarch sfantul ierarh nectarie saints and archangels 9 november ⚜9 november – the remembrance of saint nektarios of aegina⚜ • \"those who do not believe in miracles deny that god can reveal himself to the world, for a miracle is nothing other than god's revelation in the world\" (saint nektarios of aegina) • over time we have made three icons of the saint in our workshop. as the main photo i am showing you the most recent one. #sfantulnectarie", "p1057": "the holy archangels michael and gabriel sfintii arhangheli mihail si gavriil saints and archangels savu moga, arpasu de sus, 1890 8 november ⚜ on 8 november the orthodox church celebrates the synaxis of the holy archangels michael and gabriel and of all the heavenly powers, so today i am showing you the holy archangels michael and gabriel in an icon on glass painted in our workshop (model: savu moga, arpasu de sus, 1890) ◘ this feast dates from the 5th century, beginning as the simple anniversary of the consecration of the church of saint michael the archangel built at the baths of arcadius in constantinople. over time, the feast came to be dedicated to all the holy angels. the seven angels we celebrate are: • michael – translated as “the power of god”. he is the commander of the heavenly hosts and the first of the holy archangels; he carries the fiery sword, and his role is to guard the law of god and to overcome all who do not obey it. he is also the one who stopped the angels from falling from heaven, who defended the body of moses and who brought the ten plagues upon pharaoh's people. it is said that at the end of the age he will raise the dead and gather all nations to judgement. • gabriel is translated as “man of god”, being the archangel of the annunciation. he carries no fiery sword, but the lily of undefiled joy. he was the first to speak the name of jesus, the one who brought the great mystery of the lord's incarnation, the news of the conception, and who gave saint john the baptist his name. • raphael is the healer of human infirmities • uriel is the enlightener of those in darkness • selaphiel is the one who prays for mankind • jegudiel is the glorifier of god and the strengthener of those who do good works • barachiel is the bringer of god's blessing upon the earth ◘ happy name day to all who celebrate!", "p1062": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels nicula, first half of the 19th century ♦ as we wait for the feast of saint paraskeva, we are showing you one of the icons on this theme painted in our workshop (model: nicula, first half of the 19th century) ♦ father ilie cleopa: “let us honour saint paraskeva with faith and kiss her holy relics with devotion whenever we can. then let us often read her akathist, all singing to her with one voice this short prayer: ~ rejoice, saint paraskeva, our great helper! ~ “", "p793": "saint paisios the athonite sfantul cuvios paisie aghioritul saints and archangels 12 july • on 12 july the orthodox church remembers saint paisios the athonite, one of the best-known and most beloved saints of the 20th century. saint paisios was born on 25 july 1924 in farasa, cappadocia, and departed to the lord on 12 july 1994. • on this special day, i am showing you an icon on glass (of saint paisios) made in our workshop for a young family from maramures. • i am also sharing with you the testament of the venerable paisios the athonite after the death of elder paisios, a precious text in the father's own hand was found at the panagouda cell: “when i, the renowned paisios, examined myself, i saw that i had broken all the commandments of the lord and committed all the sins. it does not matter if i committed some of them to a lesser degree, for i have no extenuating circumstances at all, since i received so many blessings from the lord. pray that christ may have mercy on me. forgive me, and may all those who think they have grieved me be forgiven. thank you very much, and again, pray! the monk paisios”. (from saint paisios the athonite – evanghelismos publishing)", "p1065": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts • “jesus christ entered jerusalem carrying with him the faith of the righteous of the old testament and fulfilling the promises made to the prophets, so that salvation might pour out from jerusalem over the whole world” (bishop ambrozie) • “the entry of the lord jesus into jerusalem” – the fourth icon on this theme painted in our workshop • the icon was painted to order, so it is not available. it will be painted again only to order", "p1066": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels icon from 1887, arpasu de sus, savu moga 6 december ⚜saint nicholas the hierarch – 6 december ✧ “saint nicholas was gentle, without malice and humble in spirit, guarding himself against pride. to the poor he was a father; to the needy, merciful; a comforter to those who wept; a helper to the wronged, and a great benefactor to all” (doxologia.ro) ✧ we welcome the great feast with an icon on glass (a study after an icon from 1887, arpasu de sus, savu moga), which is in the collection of a lovely romanian family in transylvania, together with other icons painted in our workshop ✧ happy name day to all who celebrate!🌼", "p1067": "the exaltation of the holy cross inaltarea sfintei cruci jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, mid-19th century, held by the national museum of the union, alba iulia 14 september ~ 14 september: the feast of the exaltation of the holy cross ~ • \"the cross is made of our weaknesses and defeats, but the calling is clear: let us love our cross! perhaps this is the hardest act of all... to accept yourself as you are...\" (the theologian paul evdokimov) • the icon (on this theme) that i am showing you (model: nicula, mid-19th century, held by the national museum of the union, alba iulia) was painted in our workshop for a holy monastery in the heart of transylvania", "p1068": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god nicula, first half of the 19th century ... the mother of god wishes greater things for us than we wish for ourselves ... (father arsenie papacioc) • on the eve of the great feast of \"the nativity of the mother of god\", we are showing you an icon on glass on this theme, painted for a holy church (model: nicula, first half of the 19th century)", "p774": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels 14 october ⊹ 14 october: saint paraskeva, a saint always close to the hearts of christians, as a gentle comforter and a quick helper. ⊹ we welcome the feast of «saint paraskeva» by showing you one of the icons on this theme, made in our workshop for a lovely couple from bucharest. ⊹ happy name day to all who celebrate!🌺", "p1031": "the holy brancoveanu martyrs sfintii martiri brancoveni martyrs and heroes 18 february ◘ 18 february marks 71 years since the departure from earthly life of the pillar of fire of christian spirituality in the communist prisons, valeriu gafencu (whom nicolae steinhardt called “the saint of the prisons”) ◘ valeriu gafencu was born on 24 january 1921 in sangerei, bessarabia; he was one of the young intellectuals who died in the prisons of romania's communist regime of those times ◘ in this icon painted on glass (ordered as a gift to a holy church in western romania), saint valeriu gafencu is shown alongside the holy brancoveanu martyrs", "p786": "the dormition of the mother of god adormirea maicii domnului the mother of god 15 august «the dormition of the mother of god» – 15 august • we welcome the great feast of «the dormition of the mother of god» with an icon painted on glass in our workshop for a holy church. • «the icon of «the dormition of the mother of god» has a rich and deep spiritual meaning, revealing for each of us. in it we can see the falling asleep, the burial, the resurrection and the ascension of the mother of god, steps through which we too may pass. the icon of the scene of «the dormition of the mother of god» describes a lofty state of reverence of the whole universe towards the all-holy theotokos.» (fr. nicolai boian)", "p1074": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god • « the mother of god and the “burning bush” » – icon painted on glass, modelled on several depictions, one of them being the first icon (on this theme) to reach our country (in the 1940s), at the venerable foundation of saint antim the iberian, the antim monastery in bucharest. many generations of the church's servants and of the faithful have prayed before this icon, and it also inspired the well-known hesychast movement “the burning bush”, a group that kept the fire of faith alive in the hearts of many romanians, especially during the communist rule. • according to the painters' manual, the icon “the burning bush” shows a large eight-pointed star in the form of overlapping rhombuses, with the mother of god holding the saviour in her arms at their centre. four of the eight points are red, representing the fire, and the other four, coloured green, symbolise that the bush did not burn but remained whole. on the points of the red star are the symbols of the four holy evangelists: the angel (saint matthew), the lion (saint mark), the ox (saint luke) and the eagle (saint john), and on the four points of the green star the holy angels are depicted. • if you would like a similar icon, contact me and we will settle the details. this icon is not available; it was made to order.", "p981": "saint elijah the prophet sfantul proroc ilie saints and archangels workshop in scheii brasovului, second half of the 19th century 20 july on 20 july the romanian orthodox church celebrates the ascent into heaven of the holy great prophet elijah the tishbite, a saint honoured as a great wonderworker and bringer of rain in times of drought depicted in icons either at the mouth of his cave (which can still be visited today, in the land of choziba) with the ravens sent to feed him, or in the chariot of fire in which he was taken up to heaven, or in both (as in the icon shown today), the holy great prophet elijah the tishbite is the old testament figure dearest and most familiar to the christian conscience everywhere we welcome the great feast with an icon on glass made after the icon «the ascent of the holy prophet elijah into heaven, with scenes from his life» (scheii brasovului, early 19th century), in the collection of the leon sculy logothetti family of iasi happy name day to all who celebrate!🌺", "p1009": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts 1872, arpasu de sus, savu moga • \"... and we, the new and spiritual israel, prepare to welcome the lord, who comes meek and humble to enter the jerusalem of our souls ... \" (father petroniu tanase) • we welcome him with joy and with an icon painted in our workshop: «the entry of the lord into jerusalem» (model: 1872, arpasu de sus, savu moga)", "p1079": "icons painted in our workshop icoane pictate in atelierul nostru other works • some of the icons painted on glass in our workshop, together with the icon of the holy martyr valeriu gafencu (painted on wood, in another workshop), awaiting the service called \"the order for the blessing of icons\" • the icons (painted on glass) are: - saint elijah - the holy brancoveanu martyrs and saint valeriu gafencu - the presentation of the lord - the mother of god and the saints of the prisons - a feast icon with the annunciation - the burning bush of the mother of god - saint george the great martyr - the table of paradise • photo: in the home of a lovely young romanian family (2022)", "p1081": "saint nektarios the hierarch sfantul ierarh nectarie saints and archangels • \"my brothers! happiness is within you, and blessed is the man who understands this. search your hearts and see in what spiritual state you are!\" (saint nektarios of aegina) • if you would like a special icon (painted on glass) of saint nektarios, contact me and we will settle the details. the icon i am showing you is not available; it was painted to order.", "p1082": "the holy apostles peter and paul sfintii apostoli petru si pavel saints and archangels early 19th century • we welcome the great feast of the holy apostles peter and paul with the joy of showing you an icon (painted on glass after a model from the early 19th century) • the model of the church held up by the two saints (peter and paul) illustrates the words of jesus: \"you are peter, and on this rock i will build my church!\" ☼ \"happy name day\" to all who celebrate!", "p1059": "saint demetrius the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic dimitrie saints and archangels marginimea sibiului, second half of the 19th century ~ “share out your earthly wealth... let us seek the heavenly one” (saint demetrius) ~ ◙ 26 october: the feast of the holy great martyr demetrius the myrrh-streaming (dumitru), one of the great holy martyrs, a wonderworking and healing saint ◙ we welcome this great feast with an icon on glass painted in our workshop (model: marginimea sibiului, second half of the 19th century)", "p1084": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise ► the icon of “the table of paradise” (painted in our workshop) in a picturesque rustic setting, in a beautiful house in the heart of transylvania ► the theme (inspired by church painting and the lives of the saints) shows, in five rhombus-shaped medallions, the faces of jesus christ, the mother of god, a holy hierarch (here saint nicholas) and a woman saint (here saint paraskeva). the central medallion frames an oversized flower ► the icon in the photo is not available; it was painted to order ► if you would like an icon on this theme (with these two saints, or with two other saints you would like painted in the lower rhombuses), contact me and we will settle the details", "p965": "the exaltation of the holy cross inaltarea sfintei cruci jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, mid-19th century 14 september ❈ 14 september | the feast of the exaltation of the holy cross ✧ razvan codrescu: “by its vertical, the cross signifies the bond between heaven and earth, the aspiration to higher things, the uprightness of a life illumined by faith. its horizontal signifies the all-embracing embrace of the world through sacrificial love, the calling and gathering of all around the holy axis that leads to heaven. the point where they cross, where the horizontal and the vertical “commune”, signifies the essential centre of our existence, our right place in the mystery of salvation, which is possible through man's co-working in grace with god, through the joining of matter to spirit and of the created spirit (the human soul) to the uncreated spirit (the holy spirit).” ✧ the icon (model: nicula, mid-19th century) that we are showing you in honour of the great feast was given to a holy place of worship built in memory of the martyrs of the romanian communist prisons", "p1088": "the holy trinity and the coronation of the mother of god sfanta treime si incoronarea maicii domnului jesus christ and the great feasts workshop in scheii brasovului, last decades of the 19th century > the theme of this icon (model: workshop in scheii brasovului, last decades of the 19th century) is the scene of the coronation of the mother of god. the scene shows the holy trinity (the spiritual unity of the three divine persons): jesus christ carrying the cross of the crucifixion, god the father with the orb and sceptre (the insignia of the almighty), and the holy spirit (as a white dove framed by the sun) sending down his blessing. the first two hold a crown above the head of the virgin mary (kneeling, dressed in a white maphorion, with her hands crossed on her chest). the figures are ”held up” by clouds. 🤍 > this icon was made to order, so it is not available. if you would like a similar icon, contact me.", "p1090": "the descent of the holy spirit pogorarea sfantului duh jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, early 19th century (†) \"the ascension of the lord\" is the feast of the day, and today's icon on glass (model: nicula, early 19th century) shows this theme. (†) christ has ascended! \"forty days after the resurrection of christ and ten days before the descent of the holy spirit, we celebrate the bodily ascension into heaven of the incarnate son of god. the ascension of christ shows what man's destination is: the human nature he took on was fully transfigured; it was not dissolved in its union with the divine nature. if it becomes invisible after the ascension, this is due to its deification. indeed, man's purpose is not to lose himself in the world, for then the most important factor of reality would be lost. the bodily ascension into heaven is a testimony that man was created for eternity, for the son presents himself to the father as god and also as man. through his ascension, christ not only shows where man must arrive, but becomes the way and the power for man to reach that state. he sits on the divine throne of glory, yet he also dwells in the hearts of those who love him. this is how we can understand the paradox: christ is ascended, and yet on the way to ascension with each one of us...\" (crestinortodox.ro)", "p1091": "the ascension of the lord inaltarea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, 18th century \"the ascension of the lord\" (model: nicula, 18th century) – one of the first icons painted in our workshop – awaiting the great feast in a holy church!❤", "p999": "the martyrs of the communist prisons martirii din temnitele comuniste martyrs and heroes 14 may “ ...communism filled heaven with saints...\" (arsenie papacioc) 14 may: the national day of remembrance of the martyrs of the communist prisons", "p1094": "saints constantine and helen, the emperors sfintii imparati constantin si elena saints and archangels nicula, mid-19th century 21 may saints constantine and helen, the emperors – 21 may we welcome the great feast with an icon painted on glass, one of the first icons painted in our workshop (model: nicula, mid-19th century). happy name day to all who celebrate!🌺", "p949": "the entry of the mother of god into the temple intrarea in biserica a maicii domnului the mother of god savu moga, 1860 21 november ⚜ «the entry of the mother of god into the temple» (21 november) ✧ “today the virgin mary was brought to jerusalem, into the lord's temple, to pray, to speak with god and with the angels, to be deified, to become a living temple of the holy spirit, to prepare to give birth on earth to jesus christ, the saviour of the world\" (from a sermon by father cleopa) ✧ as we wait to celebrate this great feast (the first of the nativity fast), we are showing you one of the icons on this theme, an icon i painted on glass (model: savu moga, 1860) for a holy church in dobrogea", "p1097": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels laz, sebes valley, first half of the 19th century • “when things are hardest for you, call on saint nicholas for help!” (fr. i. filin) • «saint nicholas the great hierarch» – icon painted on glass in our workshop (model: laz, sebes valley, first half of the 19th century)🍂", "p1098": "saint george the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic gheorghe saints and archangels • «saint george the great martyr» in an icon painted on glass in our workshop (model: tara oltului, first half of the 19th century → a charming depiction, like a fairy tale “told” in colours painted on glass ❤) • γεωργιος, agios georgios, or george – versions: georgiu, georz, giurgiu, iorgu, from the greek georgios – was a roman general of greek origin and an officer in the guard of the roman emperor diocletian, who was sentenced to death for refusing to renounce the christian faith. as a christian martyr he later became one of the most venerated saints of christianity, and was especially venerated by the crusaders. saint george is remembered by almost all the traditional churches, usually on 23 april. he is considered the patron of many countries, regions and cities. (wikipedia)", "p1100": "the burning bush of the mother of god rugul aprins al maicii domnului the mother of god in the church of the antim monastery (on the small iconostasis by the north door of the altar), a unique icon stands humbly... it is « the burning bush », a moving creation that inspired us to make this icon (painted on glass), which we are showing you today.🥀", "p1105": "the lamentation of christ plangerea lui iisus hristos jesus christ and the great feasts arpasu de sus, 1877 • on holy and great friday we remember the crucifixion and death on the cross of the saviour jesus christ. “christ was crucified so that we might rise again, and are we to be indifferent?!” (saint paisios the athonite) •\"the sorrowful mother of god\" is the icon we are showing you on good friday, an icon painted on glass for a holy church (model: arpasu de sus, 1877)", "p1107": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts arpasu de sus, 1872 (savu moga) ~palm sunday – the entry of the lord into jerusalem~ • \" ... and we, the new and spiritual israel, prepare to welcome the lord, who comes meek and humble to enter the jerusalem of our souls ... \" (father petroniu tanase, a member of the “burning bush” movement) • on this great feast day we are showing you a new icon painted in our workshop ~ the entry of the lord into jerusalem ~ [model: arpasu de sus, 1872 (savu moga)]", "p1108": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, 18th century a painted frame or a plain one? • we usually frame an icon on glass in fir wood, discreet and delightful in its simplicity... sometimes, though, the icon is delicately “completed” by a painted frame, which adds extra charm and originality. 🌸 • for the newer friends of this page: the theme of the icon (with a painted frame) in this photo is ~ jesus with the vine ~ (model: nicula, 18th century)", "p868": "martyrs and heroes of the romanian people martiri si eroi ai neamului romanesc martyrs and heroes 10 september ✧ 2024, the year of avram iancu: avram iancu, celebrated 200 years after his birth and 152 years after his death. • avram iancu, the future national hero, was born in 1824. the exact date of his birth was not recorded, but according to the hero himself he was born \"in cherry time\". since cherries ripen later in the mountains because of the harsher climate, he may have been born in july or august. • the work i am showing you today depicts avram iancu – “the little prince of the mountains” – with crisan, closca and horea beside horea's oak. this painting on glass is inspired by a mural in the orthodox church of “the dormition of the mother of god” at the tebea memorial complex •the testament of avram iancu “my last will! the only longing of my life is to see my nation happy, for which i have worked as far as i could until now, sadly without much success; indeed, just now i see with sorrow that my hopes and the sacrifice i made are turning to nothing. i do not know how many days i may have left; a kind of foreboding seems to tell me that the future is uncertain. i therefore wish and firmly decree that after my death all my property, movable and immovable, shall pass to the benefit of the nation, to help found an academy of law, for i firmly believe that those who fight with the weapon of the law will be able to win the rights of my nation. \"", "p1110": "the nativity of the mother of god nasterea maicii domnului the mother of god nicula, early 19th century ~ the nativity of the mother of god ~ icon on glass (model: nicula, early 19th century)🌸 about the icon: \" lying on a bed above which hangs a rich curtain, saint anne has the baby girl at her feet. joachim urges her to eat from the dishes he brings. a border with the rope motif surrounds the composition. the novelty of the image lies in the way the floor is drawn, like a roof of curved tiles, which focuses all attention on joachim's gesture.\" (source of the description: national institute of heritage) ° the icon is not available; it was painted for a holy and beautiful orthodox church in romania", "p957": "the holy transylvanian confessors sfintii marturisitori ardeleni martyrs and heroes 21 october ❈ on 21 october the orthodox church celebrates the holy transylvanian confessors • we welcome the feast of the holy confessors with an icon on glass (30x42 cm) painted in our workshop. the saints depicted in this icon are: • visarion sarai – an orthodox hieromonk who was imprisoned in the fortress of kufstein, where he died confessing orthodoxy • sofronie of cioara – a romanian monk who led the second anti-catholic revolt in transylvania • oprea miclaus – a romanian peasant who travelled three times to the imperial court in vienna to present the romanians' wish to remain in the faith of their forefathers. in 1752, together with the priest moise macinic of sibiel, he was imprisoned at kufstein, where both departed to the lord • ioan of gales – a confessor priest held responsible (by the habsburg authorities in transylvania) for coordinating a resistance movement against the union with rome; he was finally imprisoned at kufstein, where he endured 24 years of detention • moise macinic of sibiel – a confessor priest who fought against the imposition of the greek catholic confession; imprisoned at kufstein • the client wished us to depict in this icon also atanasie todoran of bichigiu (celebrated on 12 november), sentenced to death by the imperial power for refusing to renounce the faith of his forefathers, for which he was broken on the wheel at the age of 104 • source: “the history of the romanian orthodox church” by rev. prof. dr. mircea pacurariu • the icon was painted to order for a lovely romanian family from transylvania", "p1115": "the annunciation buna vestire the mother of god scheii brasovului, 19th century ~ the annunciation – feast icon (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century) ~ \"who could clearly describe the emotion of the archangel gabriel, sent to announce to mary (an earthly woman living a heavenly life) that she would conceive and give birth to the creator of heaven and earth?\" source: doxologia.ro > the icon painted on glass shows (in the centre) the scene of the annunciation to the mother of god (by the archangel gabriel): that she would give birth, as a man, to the son of god. the iconographic scene is framed by a simple border that separates it from 10 panels with icons of saints and feasts: the virgin mary, the coronation of the virgin, saints john the baptist, nicholas, basil, george, constantine and helen, demetrius, gregory and peter. > the icon is not available; it will be painted again, to order.", "p1120": "the annunciation buna vestire the mother of god scheii brasovului, 19th century 25 march ✤ 25 march – the annunciation ✤ father cleopa: «who can understand what depth of humility there was in the heart of the all-holy virgin mary, who, hearing and understanding from the archangel gabriel that she would conceive of the holy spirit and give birth to the son of god, did not exalt herself in her heart, but with great humility, considering herself a simple handmaid, said: “behold the handmaid of the lord. let it be to me according to your word.”» the icon (painted on glass) shows the scene of the annunciation to the mother of god by the archangel gabriel, announcing to her that she would give birth, as a man, to the son of god. this small icon (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century) is not available; every day it lights up the icons being painted in our workshop, which came into being five years ago, on the day of the annunciation.", "p1121": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, 18th century ~ jesus with the vine – icon painted on glass (model: nicula, 18th century) ~ an icon on glass carries a double charge: the spiritual and the purely aesthetic. the icon \"jesus with the vine\" in this depiction (model: nicula, 18th century) carries a deep spiritual charge through its very theme... “i am the true vine...\" and an aesthetic charge through its vivid colours, its oversized decorations and (sometimes) its painted frame – a charge that \"comes\" from the old icons (whose models we paint after), icons that we must respect not only as objects of worship but also as historical testimonies.", "p1122": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise nicula, early 19th century the table of paradise, or the heavenly feast – icon painted on glass (model: nicula, early 19th century) the icon is not available; i will paint it for a new order. i will paint it either like this icon or (for a personalised icon) with the two saints in the lower rhombuses replaced by any other two saints. about the icon the iconographic theme divides the space of the composition into five rhombus-shaped fields, separated by bands decorated with the « rope motif ». the rope (or spiral) motif symbolises infinity. the central rhombus and the triangular fields next to the five rhombuses hold oversized floral motifs. leaning on the sides of the middle rhombus are the four rhombuses showing the guests taking part in the heavenly feast. the mother of god with the child and jesus christ blessing with his right hand are always in the upper rhombuses; the others hold other saints, in this case saint paraskeva (the most venerated of the women martyrs) and saint nicholas the hierarch.", "p1125": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts i painted this icon (whose theme is a special one) recently... \"before\" the tragedy we are all living through, directly or indirectly...", "p1126": "the mother of god with the child maica domnului cu pruncul the mother of god nicula, 18th century the mother of god with the child jesus – icon painted on glass (model: nicula, 18th century) “we kneel and pray to you / raise us up, and save us / from the waves that toss us / be a shield of strength / and a wall of salvation…” mihai eminescu – prayer", "p1127": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, 19th century jesus christ and the vine ~ icon painted on glass (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century) this icon, \"jesus – the true vine\", also known as the eucharistic christ, is (in its essence) a depiction of the lord's words recorded by john in his gospel: “i am the true vine... you are the branches.” the icon whose photo i am showing you today has gone to sibiu, \"the homeland of icons painted on glass\", so if you would like a similar icon, contact me and together we will settle the details, first of all the scheduling!", "p1129": "the ascension of the lord inaltarea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, second half of the 19th century 25 may ✤ 25 may: the ascension of the lord (heroes' day) • “... and the saviour went up into heaven, to send us the all-holy spirit... ” (mark 16:19) • the icon on glass that we are showing you in honour of this great feast was painted in our workshop for a holy church (model: nicula, second half of the 19th century)", "p1130": "jesus christ the saviour iisus hristos mantuitorul jesus christ and the great feasts ~ father cleopa: \"... to believe even though you are not fully enlightened…\" ~ the icon of the saviour jesus christ (painted by me) has been in a holy church for two years... i would never have imagined i would live such a miracle...", "p1133": "valeriu gafencu, “the saint of the prisons” valeriu gafencu, „sfantul inchisorilor” martyrs and heroes 18 february 18 february: the saint of the prisons valeriu gafencu: “do not expect happiness to come from anywhere other than from within you, where christ dwells\". 18 february marks 72 years since the departure from earthly life of the pillar of fire of christian spirituality in the communist prisons, valeriu gafencu, whom nicolae steinhardt called “the saint of the prisons”. in this icon painted on glass (22x26 cm), saint valeriu gafencu is shown alongside the holy brancoveanu martyrs. photo: in the home of a special family from transylvania.", "p814": "saint george the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic gheorghe saints and archangels arpasu de sus, early 19th century 23 april • tomorrow we celebrate saint george the great martyr, the victory-bearer, called “the spiritual springtime”. • two of the works painted in our workshop depicting saint george the great martyr are these icons painted on glass, which we are showing you today (model: arpasu de sus, early 19th century). • about the icon the scene shows the soldier saint george, born in beirut; he was an army commander under diocletian, defended the christians and was martyred in 303 ad, and he is one of the most venerated saints. he rides a white horse, dressed in armour and a cloak, with a lance that has a cross at one end, and under the horse is the dragon pierced by the lance. behind the saint, on the horse's rump, sits the boy leo of amira with a jug in his hand, which he was taking to his master in the field when saint george freed him from slavery to the bulgars. in the distance are the emperor's daughter, saved from the dragon's claws, and the emperor throwing him the keys of the city. (wikipedia) • happy name day to the friends and followers of our page whose names come from saint george!🥀", "p926": "saint charalambos the hieromartyr sfantul sfintit mucenic haralambie saints and archangels scheii brasovului, 19th century 10 february ⚜10 february: saint charalambos the hieromartyr “i feel comforted and strengthened knowing that i will spend the rest of my days watched over and protected with boundless tenderness by saint charalambos, from the window of his icon, which comes from the peasant world so dear to me. a friend of christ and, i hope, a friend of mine, in a constant and beneficent work…” (costion nicolescu) today we welcome the great feast with costion nicolescu's wonderful words about saint charalambos and his icon on glass – and, of course, with an icon from the peasant world made in our workshop (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century). about the icon the icon shows saint charalambos binding the plague, and so saving the city. charalambos is shown in the usual way (standing, dressed in robe, mantle and omophorion, with the holy book and halo, giving a blessing), trampling the plague, which is bound by a chain fastened to his belt. the plague, carrying a scythe, has the face of a horned man. on either side of the saint, in the background, the image is enriched by a cityscape with palaces and fortified walls. the ground is rendered by bands of colour bearing hatching, crosses and flowers. from high in the sky the scene is watched over by jesus, who blesses him, and by an angel holding out a wreath of flowers to him. they are seated on clouds. on the light-blue background are large unoutlined flowers and yellow, white and black stars (source of the description: the national museum of art of romania)", "p1139": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, late 18th century ~ the nativity of the lord – the first version ~ two approaches to the same theme... a few days ago i showed you the second version of this theme; today i am showing you the first, as i promised. both icons are painted on glass – model: nicula, late 18th century.", "p1144": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels laz, sebes valley, first half of the 19th century ~ saint nicholas the great hierarch ~ – icon painted on glass (model: laz, sebes valley, first half of the 19th century) – \"saint nicholas was gentle, without malice and humble in spirit, guarding himself against pride. to the poor he was a father; to the needy, merciful; a comforter to those who wept; a helper to the wronged, and a great benefactor to all.\" (source: doxologia.ro)", "p1146": "simeon the righteous dreptul simeon saints and archangels 3 february saint simeon the righteous, celebrated in the orthodox calendar on 3 february, is also called “the god-receiver” (for what he did on the day of the feast of the presentation of the lord.) today we honour the day when the elder simeon (moved by the holy spirit) also came to the temple, where (before his death) his hope of seeing the messiah with his own eyes was fulfilled, as had been promised to him. i am showing you the first version of the icon on the theme of \"the presentation of the lord\", also painted on glass after the same model (nicula) as the second version i showed you yesterday. ~ an icon whose theme is \"the elder simeon receiving the child jesus\". ~ these icons are not available. i will paint a new version only to order.", "p1149": "the presentation of the lord intampinarea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, second half of the 19th century the presentation of the lord – icon painted on glass the theme of this icon (model: nicula, second half of the 19th century) is \"the presentation in the temple\", an event closely linked to the theme of purification and redemption. forty days after christmas we celebrate the presentation of the lord. jesus christ is brought to the temple in jerusalem by the holy virgin mary and joseph the righteous to fulfil the rules of the old law (the law of moses), which required that, 40 days after the birth of a first child, the child be presented at the temple in jerusalem with an offering to redeem the firstborn, who in fact belonged to god. the offering was a lamb and a dove. the poor, who had no lamb, could bring two young pigeons (one of which symbolised the offering of thanks to god for the gift received, while the other was the price of redemption for the child, who would otherwise have had to dedicate his life to the service of god).", "p1151": "saint george the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic gheorghe saints and archangels tara oltului, first half of the 19th century ~ saint george the martyr – icon painted on glass ~ the theme of this icon is saint george the great martyr, in a special iconographic depiction (model: tara oltului, first half of the 19th century). this saint was a roman soldier of greek origin and an officer in the guard of the roman emperor diocletian. he was sentenced to death for refusing to renounce the christian faith. as a christian martyr he later became one of the most venerated saints of christianity, and was especially venerated by the crusaders. saint george is remembered by almost all the traditional churches, usually on 23 april. he is considered the patron of many countries, regions and cities all over the world. ~ the icon is not available; i will paint it to order ~.", "p1156": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts the icon \"the nativity of the lord jesus christ\", painted again (a little different from the version i showed you recently on this page, but made after the same model, nicula), has gone to oradea, where it was a special housewarming gift.🌺", "p1158": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels nicula, first half of the 19th century ~ saint paraskeva – icon painted on glass (model: nicula, first half of the 19th century) ~ a small, delicate icon makes a special gift for any occasion. the icon in the photo is not available; i will paint a new version to order!", "p1123": "the holy archangels michael and gabriel sfintii arhangheli mihail si gavriil saints and archangels maierii, alba iulia, 18th century the holy archangels michael and gabriel – icon painted on glass holy archangels, pray for us! i painted you in this icon with awe; i ask you, also with awe, to protect us... us, our ukrainian neighbours, and all those near the place where history has stopped in shock... many abbots and spiritual fathers urge the faithful, in this dark time of history, to say the prayer to saint michael the archangel: \"defend me from earthquakes, floods, wars and every evil...\" we too ask him to defend us...", "p1162": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, early 19th century jesus – the true vine (model: scheii brasovului, early 19th century) – icon painted on glass ~the iconographic scene shows the risen jesus christ before the cross (standing on the holy table of the altar), and from his side grows a vine (full of grapes), which christ's hand presses straight into the holy chalice. from the image one can easily deduce that the icon does not aim to highlight the metaphor of the vine, frequent in the new testament writings, but what we find in the holy chalice, namely: \"in the form of the wine flowing from the grapes is the very blood of christ (truly), for the vine grows and is nourished from his side. and on the holy table of the altar lies the very body of the risen christ\".~", "p1163": "the sorrowful mother of god maica domnului indurerata the mother of god nicula, first half of the 19th century one of the first icons i painted (2019) was the icon i am showing you today. the theme of this icon (model: nicula, first half of the 19th century) is the sorrowful face of the virgin mary in the foreground, with the image of the crucifixion of jesus in the background. the event took place in the 1st century, and christians understand it as the crucifixion of the messiah, in the person of jesus of nazareth. his arrest, trial and condemnation by the roman prefect pontius pilate are described by the four gospels. the icon is not available. i will paint it again to order.", "p1164": "the sorrowful mother of god maica domnului indurerata the mother of god icon on glass – ”the sorrowful mother of god” in the painting of icons on glass, it can be said that this type of composition (the theme of the sorrowful mother of god) was born in transylvania. this theme is (in fact) the most frequent in transylvanian iconography. the version that became classic throughout transylvania is the one in which the mother of god stands with her hands joined in prayer, looking towards the cross of the crucifixion, painted in miniature in the background. one of the versions of this theme (and one of the most beautiful) was painted in arpasu de jos in 1877; after its model i painted the icon whose photo you see here: a traditional romanian icon made in the style of the icons painted by the transylvanian icon painters of the 18th–19th centuries, respecting the techniques of this art form. about the icon: painted on glass in several layers, using tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the ink drawing is fixed and protected with varnish, and the finished painting has a protective layer. the stained fir frame is also handmade. icon size: 21x29 cm (without frame); 27.55x35.5 cm (with frame) > the icon is not available (it is in a beautiful and holy church). i will paint it again only to order.", "p1166": "the holy apostles peter and paul sfintii apostoli petru si pavel saints and archangels transylvanian workshop, early 19th century saints peter and paul – icon on glass (model: transylvanian workshop, early 19th century) the theme of this icon is the apostles peter and paul. in orthodox iconography, saints peter and paul (the first and the last among the apostles) stand for the church, or the communion of israel (peter) with all the peoples of the world (paul). the model of the church held up by the two saints illustrates the words of jesus: \"you are peter, and on this rock i will build my church\" about the icon: this traditional romanian icon is made in the style of the icons painted by the transylvanian icon painters of the 18th–19th centuries, respecting the techniques of this art form (ink drawing with a calligraphy pen; painting in egg-emulsion tempera; decorative elements in gold leaf). it is a small icon (with a stand on the frame and hangers), perfect as a special gift (painted glass: 12x17 cm; framed icon: 17x22 cm).", "p1165": "saint nektarios the hierarch sfantul ierarh nectarie saints and archangels saint nektarios again... in a holy church", "p1168": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels cartisoara, second half of the 18th century saint nicholas – icon painted on glass most of the icons painted by the unique and wonderful transylvanian icon painters of the 18th–19th centuries are made like fantastic painted fairy tales, in which the saints \"meet\" harmoniously with earthly people caught in their daily activities. this icon too (model: cartisoara, second half of the 18th century) is like a gentle story told \"by the fireside\": saint nicholas is shown as a high prelate, holding the scripture in his right hand and blessing with his left. beside him are the three girls (and their father) who, according to the legend, were brought onto the right path through the help the saint gave them. in the background (on clouds) are jesus and the mother of god. saint nicholas, or “the wonderworker”, celebrated by christians on 6 december, lived in the late 3rd and early 4th centuries. he was born into a wealthy family in patara, in the province of lycia, in the asian part of today's turkey. from childhood he showed exceptional faith, and in his youth he stood out for his fine conduct, fasting, discernment and intense spiritual life. he studied at the best schools, where he stood out for his intelligence, and in the churches he entered he amazed everyone with his gentleness and nobility of soul. since his uncle was bishop of patara, nicholas spent some time at the monastery there, where he became a priest. saint nicholas worked miracles even during his lifetime. on a journey to the holy land, a violent storm frightened those on the ship, but nicholas urged everyone to pray to god, and the storm stopped. at the same time, saint nicholas raised a young sailor who had fallen from the mast and drowned. in alexandria, too, saint nicholas healed many who were sick or possessed. he saved the city of myra (also in lycia) from famine by appearing in a dream to an italian merchant and urging him to come and sell his wheat there. because of the miracles he worked, saint nicholas is considered the protector of children, especially poor children, and also of sailors, bakers, unmarried girls and the unjustly accused. saint nicholas is celebrated on 6 december by both the orthodox and the roman catholic church. the relics of saint nicholas are kept in the basilica of bari, in italy, in a crypt from which a colourless liquid flows, called “manna” or “holy manna”. according to tradition, the bishop of this diocese mixes this liquid with water, blesses it and gives it to the faithful. part of the relics of saint nicholas are at the church of saint george the new in bucharest, at kilometre zero. many places of worship also bear the name of saint nicholas.", "p1171": "the coronation of the mother of god incoronarea maicii domnului the mother of god transylvanian workshop (marginimea sibiului) icon on glass ”the coronation of the mother of god” – model: transylvanian workshop (marginimea sibiului), mid-19th century >this icon is the only one in the last two years that i painted for myself, for my soul (i “slipped it in” between orders and painted it in record time). i love this theme, i love this icon... i hope it will be cherished and loved in sibiu (where it went recently, after i showed it to you here, in the workshop)...", "p1172": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels nicula, 18th century saint paraskeva – icon on glass (model: nicula, 18th century) she too has left (together with another icon) for a holy place, where she will stand beside many of the icons i have painted. a moving place, full of faith, humility and beauty...", "p1173": "saints cyril and nicetas sfintii chiril si nichita saints and archangels ~ icon painted on glass (saint cyril and saint nicetas) ~ > orthodox calendar, 18 march 2022. it is a feast day on which saint cyril is remembered and his prayer to the holy trinity for the enlightenment of the mind and the healing of the body is said! (i painted the two saints together in an icon ordered for two little brothers.) > an article by fr. stefan sfarghie – 18 march 2022: saint cyril (†386) came from the region of jerusalem and was born in the time of emperor constantine the great (306–337) to christian parents. he was 12 years old at the time of the first ecumenical council of nicaea, in 325. in those days, the place of golgotha and the wood of the holy cross were being discovered in jerusalem, and by order of the emperor the church of the holy sepulchre and the church of the resurrection were being built. saint cyril served in the church of the resurrection in his youth, and it was in this church that he delivered his famous catecheses, or lectures, preparing for baptism those who wished to become christians. around the year 350, when his bishop maximus died, saint cyril was chosen bishop of the holy city. the following year the sign of the holy cross appeared in the sky over jerusalem, and the saint informed emperor constantius about it in detail. then hard days began for the church of christ, and the arian emperors constantius and valens, together with the arian bishops, managed twice to remove saint cyril, the defender of the apostolic dogmas, from his see. after more than 16 years of exile, towards the end of his life, saint cyril returned to his diocese. shepherding his rational flock with love and leaving the church the treasure of his 24 catecheses and the example of his life, he fell asleep in the lord after taking part in the second ecumenical council of constantinople in 381.", "p1174": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise nicula, 19th century \"the table of paradise\" or \"the heavenly feast\" in an icon painted on glass (model: nicula, 19th century) is a theme i have been asked for many, many times. one of the versions i have painted is this one, which i am showing you today. the icon is not available; a new version will be painted to order!", "p1175": "jesus christ, king and great high priest iisus hristos imparat si mare arhiereu jesus christ and the great feasts tara barsei, second half of the 19th century another version of the icon ”jesus christ, king and great high priest, flanked by archangels” (model: tara barsei, second half of the 19th century). the icon is not available; it will be painted again only to order.", "p1176": "saint nikephoros the leper sfantul nichifor leprosul saints and archangels ~saint nikephoros the leper, with scenes from his life~ the icon (my own composition) is not available; it will be painted again only to order. the icon i am showing you today is painted on glass (30x42 cm) in the traditional technique. doxologia.ro: the venerable nikephoros the leper was born on the island of crete into a family of devout peasants and was orphaned at an early age. at thirteen, the first signs of the “holy disease”, as leprosy is called in the church of christ, appeared on his body. to escape the permanent isolation that awaited him, he took refuge for a time in egypt. at twenty-four he arrived at the leper colony on chios, in the care of saint anthimos of chios, where he was tonsured a monk. there, for forty-one years, although more and more crippled by the disease, he gave himself with a martyr's patience to struggles beyond nature, becoming an example for his brothers in suffering. after the cure for leprosy was discovered in 1947, the leper colony on chios was closed and the venerable one was moved to the saint barbara hospital in athens. blind and confined to his sickbed, yet endowed with many divine gifts, he spent the last years of his life giving hope to the despairing, comfort to the suffering and zeal to the young. at the age of seventy-four the holy leper departed this world; later, the finding of his holy relics and the countless healings he still works today showed him to be one of the greatest intercessors of our times. in 2012 the ecumenical patriarchate glorified saint nikephoros the leper, with his feast on 4 january, the day of his falling asleep.", "p1177": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts an icon painted on glass (whatever its theme) is a special gift that will be received with immense joy by those who know this \"corner\" of iconography. it will be received (this gift) with wonder by those who have never seen a \"naive\" icon, so \"cheerful\" in its colours and decorations. with wonder, but with delight and curiosity too. this gift will be honoured, respected and loved by whoever receives it, because they will receive it with reverence, kind thoughts and gratitude. the gift idea i am suggesting today is a \"detail\" from the icon jesus – the true vine. the icon is painted on glass, 10x15 cm, and the \"rustic\" frame can be replaced by an ordinary fir frame. this icon is not available; it will be painted only to order.", "p1178": "saint stylianos of paphlagonia sfantul cuvios stelian paflagonul saints and archangels 26 november ⚜saint stylianos of paphlagonia⚜ ✧ one of the saints closest to children is celebrated in november, on the 26th. he is saint stylianos of paphlagonia, considered the protector of infants and of the christian family. his life of prayer and his love of god made him worthy of the gift of working miracles, especially healing sick children. ✧ the icon i am showing you today – adorned with flowers for the patronal feast of a holy and beautiful church in dobrogea – was painted in our workshop, in the traditional technique.", "p1179": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god in a place of honour – in the \"place of worship\" – stand a few icons i painted! two of them (painted in 2020) are these: the mother of god and the saviour! one of the happiest days was the day the church's priest sent me the photos! then came only bright days...", "p1180": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise an icon painted on glass is an object of worship in the eastern church and in the orthodox christian's home. it can also be a special gift! an unusual gift idea would be the icon of “the table of paradise” (which so many of you liked on this page) – a rhombus-shaped table showing the virgin mary, the saviour jesus christ and two saints. usually the two saints are saint nicholas and saint paraskeva. in the icon i am showing you today (as a gift suggestion), saint george the great martyr is painted in the rhombus where saint nicholas usually is, and the icon was ordered as a gift for someone special! of course, the two saints can be replaced by any other saint (or saints)!", "p1181": "the burning bush of the mother of god rugul aprins al maicii domnului the mother of god the burning bush – icon painted on glass \"the burning bush is the symbol of unceasing prayer: whoever prays unceasingly is like this bush that burned and was not consumed. we are always under the fire of god – this blaze of light and power – and the more it burns, the brighter we become and the closer to god. that is one meaning of the burning bush.\" father sofian boghiu under the name “the burning bush of the mother of god”, a christian and cultural society was active at the antim monastery in bucharest (between 1946 and 1948) which regarded prayer as one of the paths to salvation. the initiator and driving force of this society was the poet and journalist sandu tudor, who became a monk under the name daniil. together with a group of lay intellectuals and monks (a group that wished to preserve the true orthodox faith and orthodox values in times of atheist communism), he founded a christian and cultural society that regarded prayer as one of the paths to salvation. the association's name was “the burning bush” – the bush which, according to the bible, burns with an ever-green flame and which symbolises the union of the saved soul with the absolute. sandu tudor brought an old icon from mount athos dedicated to the burning bush, an icon from which i dared to take inspiration in painting the icon i am showing you today. the icon is not available; i will paint it again only to order.", "p1182": "the mother of god maica domnului the mother of god fr. cleopa: \"have great devotion, brothers, to the virgin mary! blessed is the house and the family that has the icon of the mother of god in the home\"", "p1186": "the baptism of the lord botezul domnului jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, first half of the 19th century the baptism of the lord jesus christ – icon painted on glass the theme of this icon (the most recent icon i have painted on this theme) is the baptism of the lord. the sacrament of holy baptism is the sacrament of being born again, the sacrament of a person's spiritual birth. through biological or bodily birth, man is born for this earthly life and goes towards death because of ancestral sin, which has been passed on to all people as a predisposition or inclination to sin. so whoever is born physically in adam, as a human being, is born to die physically; but whoever is born spiritually in christ, through baptism with water and the holy spirit, is born to live forever, according to the saviour's words: “whoever believes in me, though he die, yet shall he live”. the baptism of the lord jesus christ (theophany) is celebrated today, 6 january. in the depiction of the baptism in this icon (model: scheii brasovului, first half of the 19th century) jesus is in the middle, standing in the waters of the jordan; on his right is john the baptist, and on his left the angel holding the cloth. above, the holy spirit is shown in the form of a dove.", "p1187": "the baptism of the lord botezul domnului jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, 19th century the baptism of the lord jesus christ – icon painted on glass the theme of the baptism of the lord, one of the great events of christendom, also called theophany, epiphany or the divine manifestation, holds an important place in the peasant icons on glass. the icon (painted after a model from scheii brasovului, 19th century) shows jesus christ in a humble attitude, with his hands crossed on his chest, at the moment he is baptised by his forerunner, the great prophet john. also in a humble attitude is an angel of the lord, holding a towel in both hands as the lord comes out of the waters of the jordan.) the icon is painted on glass in several layers, using tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the ink drawing is fixed and protected with varnish, and the finished painting has a protective layer of colour with linseed oil. the stained fir frame is also handmade. icon size: 21x29 cm (without frame); 27.55x35.5 cm (with frame) epiphany, or theophany (from the greek theophania, meaning “the appearance / manifestation of god”), is one of the great feasts of the orthodox church, celebrated on 6 january. on this day we celebrate the baptism of the lord jesus christ by saint john the baptist in the river jordan and the beginning of christ's early preaching. the feast of epiphany marks the end of the christmas celebrations, which begin on 25 december and end on 6 january. during the service of this feast, the great blessing of the waters takes place; the holy water is used by priests to bless the homes of the faithful. the feast is called theophany because at the baptism of christ the holy trinity appeared to the world for the first time: the voice of the father is heard from heaven, the son is incarnate and stands in the river jordan, and the holy spirit descends upon him in the form of a dove. the icon is not available; it will be painted again to order!", "p1188": "jesus christ, king and great high priest iisus hristos imparat si mare arhiereu jesus christ and the great feasts workshop in tara barsei, second half of the 19th century icon on glass, ”jesus christ, king and great high priest, flanked by archangels”. model: workshop in tara barsei, second half of the 19th century description pen-and-ink drawing on glass, fixed with varnish. painting: tempera, egg emulsion and linseed oil; final protective layer (on the back): oil colours and linseed oil. the icon is painted on glass, 21 x 29 cm. stained fir frame. details the icon is painted “in mirror image” (partly reconstructed) after a model from tara barsei, second half of the 19th century. the icon is not available; it will be painted to order. why christ is high priest, teacher and king (source: “40 orthodox theses about god and the salvation of man” – the newspaper rasunetul) jesus christ is the supreme teacher or prophet by his very person; as a teacher he is not like any other man, and as a prophet he surpasses all who came before him, because he stands on another plane. his teaching is unique, because he is unique, and he is one with his teaching, which springs from him. “learn from me, for i am meek and lowly in heart, and you will find rest for your souls.” jesus christ is the supreme prophecy and the culminating revelation, and here we find what is to be known about god and man in all its fullness. the word of jesus christ is the living truth and is identical with his person, for he became the hypostasis of the human spirit. the person of jesus christ and the kingdom of god that he preaches, preaching himself, are an absolute and final newness; here lies the infinity of life, this kingdom of god being the one and only chance of eternal life. jesus christ speaks to people as god, and also as man. he communicates to them the word of god, but he also communicates his answer as man to god, for he prays for them and teaches them to pray. his teaching calls us to answer him, while at the same time it glorifies god. as high priest, jesus christ offers himself as a sacrifice, and this ministry is directed straight to god the father, but it is also directed towards us, because he wishes to include us in it. jesus christ offers as a sacrifice the human nature he took on, so this high-priestly ministry also has its effect on the human nature he assumed. christ's sacrifice was made for the restoration of human nature in him, for the deification of this nature in him. christ's sacrifice restores communion between god and man. that is why jesus christ is always in a state of sacrifice, giving himself wholly to the father while at the same time having compassion on us. that is why he is the supreme high priest, because he is also god; that is why christ intercedes for us with the father. man wishes to enter into communion with god, and god accepts him because man wishes and strives not to sin any more; so god's acceptance comes not because man suffers a punishment for his sin, but, as i said before, because of his sincere efforts to leave the realm of sin. jesus christ is king, and the saviour is raised to this full royal power through his resurrection, his ascension and his sitting at the right hand of the father, from where he guides the work of salvation and from where he will come in great glory to judge the world. the saviour's resurrection shows and proves that history is destined to be raised to another plane, higher than its present one: the plane of incorruptible life, where there is no death, where the freedom of the human spirit, through the holy spirit, makes the body transparent.", "p1194": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts arpasu de sus, tara oltului, 1872 (savu moga) the entry into jerusalem – icon painted on glass an authentic, framed, traditional romanian icon, made in the style of the icons painted by the transylvanian icon painters of the 18th–19th centuries, respecting the techniques of this art form. model: arpasu de sus, tara oltului, 1872 (savu moga) painted on glass in several layers, using tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the ink drawing is fixed and protected with varnish, and the finished painting has a protective layer of colour with linseed oil. the stained fir frame is also handmade. icon size: 30x43 cm (without frame); 37x50 cm (with frame) the theme of this icon is \"the entry of the lord into jerusalem\", also known as \"palm sunday\". the entry of the lord into jerusalem, also known as palm sunday, is one of the great feasts of the orthodox church, celebrated on the sunday before easter. a few days before his crucifixion, the lord jesus christ was welcomed, as the messiah and king of israel, by the crowds who glorified and honoured him as he entered jerusalem riding on the foal of a donkey. in their joy, the crowds threw palm or fig leaves before him, the symbol of victory, and even the children cried out words of praise to him. traditions orthodox christians celebrate this day as a joyful one, but with the understanding that the days that follow are days of sorrow. orthodox christians in countries where palms and figs do not grow, such as the romanians or the russians, use willow branches instead for this feast. the faithful bring to church these branches of willow, fig or palm (also called, by an older name, “stalpari”, hence the romanian name of the feast, “duminica stalparilor”), recalling those with which the saviour was welcomed as he entered jerusalem. at the end of the holy liturgy, the priest says a prayer of blessing over them, sprinkles them with holy water to sanctify them, and then gives them to the faithful, who adorn their icons with them and keep them with care. in some churches it is the custom, after the liturgy, to give out small crosses made of palm leaves, which are then placed by the icons. on the eve of the feast, in some places a pilgrimage or procession is held, which always starts from one church and ends at (another) church. in this way the people's going out to meet the lord on his way to jerusalem is remembered, and the pilgrimage itself also serves to bless the place. > the icon is not available; i will paint it to order", "p1199": "saint nektarios the hierarch sfantul ierarh nectarie saints and archangels sometimes we are blessed with miracles that come into our lives suddenly, like gifts from the divine, who smiles on us indulgently as we stand amazed... not many miracles have happened in my life; there have been few, but they were overwhelming! the most recent one happened almost 3 years ago, on the day of the annunciation, a holy day on which i began to paint icons on glass. i didn't know much about the icons painted on glass by our wonderful transylvanian peasants, about their soul, about their technique, unique in the world, of painting religious scenes in vivid colours, with oversized decorations and in images that blended their real lives with biblical scenes... and i had never painted until that day! it was the beginning! since then i have painted almost 80 icons, which are now mostly in private collections of public figures and ordinary people (all of them remarkable people), and in a few churches and monasteries in romania. i thank the lord for this miracle in my life and for giving an extraordinary meaning to the rest of my life!", "p1197": "the sorrowful mother of god maica domnului indurerata the mother of god in painting on glass, it can be said that this type of composition (the theme of the sorrowful mother of god) was born in transylvania. this theme is (in fact) the most frequent in transylvanian iconography. the version that became classic throughout transylvania is the one in which the mother of god stands with her hands joined in prayer, looking towards the cross of the crucifixion, painted in miniature in the background. one of the versions of this theme (and one of the most beautiful) was painted in arpasu de jos in 1877; after its model i painted the icon whose photos you see here: an authentic, framed, traditional romanian icon, made in the style of the icons painted by the transylvanian icon painters of the 18th–19th centuries, respecting the techniques of this art form. painted on glass in several layers, using tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the ink drawing is fixed and protected with varnish, and the finished painting has a protective layer. the stained fir frame is also handmade. size: 21x29 cm (without frame); 27.55x35.5 cm (with frame). the icon is available to order.", "p1183": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului the icon \"jesus – the true vine\", also known as \"the eucharistic christ\", is unique in the world. a beauty that came from the hands of anonymous makers, simple peasants (from a transylvania under foreign rule), who through their icons painted on glass upheld orthodoxy with an immense faith in god and in his works. the icon on this theme is considered to be the orthodox romanians' answer to the calvinist question. they generally painted it in a naive manner, charmingly balanced by the native artistic sense of these transylvanian peasants! it was made exclusively on glass, in most of the renowned schools of transylvania: nicula, scheii brasovului, gherla, maierii (alba iulia), lancram, fagaras, marginimea sibiului. specialists say that ~the icon is a depiction of the lord's words recorded by john in his gospel: “i am the true vine...”, and it is found above all in the altar area, at the table of oblation, where the bread and wine are prepared for communion. the vine pouring out of jesus's body refers to the moment when the wine is changed into the blood of the lord during the holy liturgy.~ i have painted this theme, \"jesus – the true vine\", in two versions. one of them (painted after a model from scheii brasovului) is at the top of clients' requests, so i have painted it very many times, but always with the same joy. the second version (painted after a nicula model) is the icon i am showing you today.", "p1167": "saint elijah the prophet sfantul proroc ilie saints and archangels transylvanian workshop, early 19th century icon on glass – ”the ascent of the holy prophet elijah into heaven, with scenes from his life” – (model: transylvanian workshop, early 19th century). on 20 july (in midsummer) there is a religious feast awaited with a certain trepidation, because it is most often accompanied by lightning, thunder and torrential rain: saint elijah the tishbite, the prophet. elijah is above all a symbolic figure of identity: the only man to whom the divine power was given to “shut and open the heavens”, the only prophet who appears in the gospel of jesus, on mount tabor, beside moses and jesus in all the glory of the godhead, knowing god face to face, the man of prayer par excellence. he is recognised as a continuer of monotheism in general and as the forerunner of the second coming of christ. elijah is the best known of the prophets of the bible. he is the only prophet venerated by the three great religions of the world: judaism, islam and christianity. the prophet elijah holds an important place in jewish and islamic mysticism, and also in orthodox hesychasm: he is the invisible spiritual master who speaks to those called to a direct relationship with the divine world. elijah is the biblical hero who still influences the whole of culture today, being, par excellence, the whole world's meteorologist on duty.\" about the icon: i painted this icon – after a 19th-century transylvanian model – in the traditional technique. the icon shows the classic scene of saint elijah appearing in the chariot of fire. in the upper part, this chariot appears in the sky, drawn by two red winged horses. the saint stands in the chariot, holding the reins in one hand and in the other the whip with which he drives the horses. the chariot is surrounded by flames. in the lower part, on the ground, saint elijah is shown fed by the ravens, and elisha, with his hands joined in prayer, awaiting saint elijah's mantle. > the icon is not available; i will paint it to order.", "p1134": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, 19th century jesus with the vine – icon painted on glass (model: scheii brasovului, 19th century) – the icon is not available; i will paint it again only to order. – in romanian iconography there is a theme unique in the originality of its allegorical vision. it is jesus with the vine (which grows out of his very body), as it appears only in the romanian icons of transylvania. it is called “the icon of the eucharist” and is considered the most beloved icon of christ (in transylvania). the source of this special depiction is christ's words: \"i am the true vine...\" (john 15:1). the icon belongs to the altar area, where the bread and wine are prepared for the holy liturgy, that is, for communion. christ is shown seated on a (dowry) chest [a chest brilliantly linked by the transylvanian icon painters with the \"dowry\" of the ancestral faith] before the cross. from his side grows a vine stem full of bunches of grapes, which surrounds him like a halo, and with his hands christ presses the grapes into a cup, suggesting the changing of the wine into the blood of the lord during the holy liturgy, and christ as the source of the life-giving \"wine\".", "p1113": "jesus christ, king and great high priest iisus hristos imparat si mare arhiereu jesus christ and the great feasts icon from tara barsei (1802) • «jesus christ, king and great high priest, flanked by archangels» – icon on glass (22x26 cm), a study after an icon from tara barsei (1802) • the icon is not available", "a8": "the baptism of the lord botezul domnului jesus christ and the great feasts", "a5": "the mother of god with the child maica domnului cu pruncul the mother of god", "a3": "the annunciation buna vestire the mother of god", "a20": "the holy apostles peter and paul sfintii apostoli petru si pavel saints and archangels", "a2": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise", "a19": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels", "a18": "saint george the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic gheorghe saints and archangels", "a17": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels", "a16": "saint charalambos the hieromartyr sfantul sfintit mucenic haralambie saints and archangels", "a15": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels", "a14": "the burning bush of the mother of god rugul aprins al maicii domnului the mother of god", "a13": "the nativity of the mother of god nasterea maicii domnului the mother of god", "a12": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts", "a10": "the entry of the lord into jerusalem intrarea domnului in ierusalim jesus christ and the great feasts", "a1": "the baptism of the lord botezul domnului jesus christ and the great feasts", "a0": "the annunciation buna vestire the mother of god", "v25": "saint cyprian and saint stephen sfantul ciprian si sfantul stefan saints and archangels", "v24": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts", "v23": "the exaltation of the holy cross inaltarea sfintei cruci jesus christ and the great feasts 14 september", "v22": "the resurrection of the lord invierea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts", "v17": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, early 19th century jesus – the true vine is a theme found in the transylvanian peasant icons, evoking the mystery of holy communion. the icon illustrates the parable of the vine: “i am the vine, you are the branches”. jesus presented himself as the true vine, his father as the vinedresser who planted it, and his disciples as the branches of this vine. it is an archetype according to which the essential elements of life – food, healing and worship – grew out of the primordial sacrifice. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v16": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, early 19th century jesus – the true vine is a theme found in the transylvanian peasant icons, evoking the mystery of holy communion. the icon illustrates the parable of the vine: “i am the vine, you are the branches”. jesus presented himself as the true vine, his father as the vinedresser who planted it, and his disciples as the branches of this vine. it is an archetype according to which the essential elements of life – food, healing and worship – grew out of the primordial sacrifice. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v15": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels nicula, 1867 6 december the theme of this icon (nicula, 1867) is saint nicholas, celebrated on 6 december by both the orthodox and the roman catholic church. saint nicholas is considered the protector of children, especially poor children, and also of sailors, bakers, unmarried girls and the unjustly accused. the tradition of giving gifts began with him. he was born in the second half of the 3rd century into a wealthy family, in patara, in the province of lycia, in the asian part of today's turkey. from his youth he felt a calling to the spiritual life. left without parents, he used the fortune he inherited to help the poor and to build a church. the relics of saint nicholas are kept in bari, in italy, in a crypt from which a colourless liquid flows, called “manna”. according to tradition, the local bishop mixes this liquid with water, blesses it and gives it to the faithful. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v18": "the mother of god with the child maica domnului cu pruncul the mother of god the usual model of the icon of the virgin and child, found in both east and west, is the virgin holding the child. it contains more than the mother of god as a person: it is an image and an affirmation of the incarnation and its reality, an affirmation of the virgin's true and real motherhood. if you look carefully at the icon, you will see that the mother of god, holding the child, never looks at him. nor does she look at you, or into the distance: her eyes are always turned inward, in contemplation. her tenderness is expressed by the shyness of her hands. she holds the child without embracing him, as one would hold something holy brought as an offering, and all the tenderness, all the human love, is expressed by the child, not by the mother. she remains the mother of god and behaves towards the child not as towards an ordinary child, but as towards the incarnate son of god, who became the son of the virgin; and he, being true man and true god, shows her all the love and tenderness of man and of god. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v14": "the holy apostles peter and paul sfintii apostoli petru si pavel saints and archangels nicula, early 19th century 29 june in orthodox iconography, saints peter and paul (the first and the last among the apostles) stand for the church, or the communion of israel (peter) with all the peoples of the world (paul). the model of the church held up by the two saints illustrates the words of jesus: “you are peter, and on this rock i will build my church”. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v13": "adam and eve in paradise adam si eva in rai jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, second half of the 19th century according to the book of genesis (the first book of the old testament and of the bible), adam and eve were the first man and the first woman created by god. the moment when the two break the divine commandment and taste from the tree of knowledge is a frequent theme in iconography. this theme also attracted the transylvanian icon painters, who painted the famous old testament scene on glass. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v12": "saint george the great martyr sfantul mare mucenic gheorghe saints and archangels nicula, early 19th century 23 april the theme of this icon is saint george the great martyr. he was a roman soldier of greek origin, an officer in the guard of emperor diocletian, sentenced to death for refusing to renounce the christian faith. as a martyr, he later became one of the most venerated saints of christendom. he is remembered by almost all the traditional churches, usually on 23 april, and is considered the protector of many countries, regions and cities all over the world. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v11": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels nicula, first half of the 19th century 14 october the theme of this icon is saint paraskeva the new, or paraskeva of iasi, a saint honoured throughout the orthodox church, especially in romania, serbia, greece and bulgaria. in romania she is considered the protector of moldavia and is the most popular of all the saints whose relics lie in the country. hundreds of parish churches are dedicated to her. among the people she is also known as saint friday. her feast is on 14 october, when tens of thousands of people come to iasi every year to venerate her holy relics. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v9": "the mother of god crowned as queen maica domnului imparatita the mother of god scheii brasovului, 1780 the icon of the mother of god (scheii brasovului, 1780) depicts the first human being to fulfil the purpose of the incarnation: the deification of man. it is one of the crowned images of the queen of the angels, with the holy child at her breast and the angels placing the crown on her head. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v8": "the mother of god with the child maica domnului cu pruncul the mother of god northern transylvania, mid-19th century specialists say that this icon painted on glass (thought to come from the mid-19th century, in northern transylvania) is a combination of orthodox and catholic elements. icon painters of every age have tried to show the mother of god as beautiful, gentle, dignified and glorified as possible. sometimes they painted her saddened, sometimes sorrowful, but always full of spiritual strength and wisdom. the all-pure one is always shown with her head covered by a veil falling onto her shoulders, according to the jewish tradition of those times. in most icons, the mother of god holds the child on her left arm and points to him with her right hand; this icon, painted on anti-reflective glass, is one of the versions in which the child is held in her right hand. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v7": "saints constantine and helen, the emperors sfintii imparati constantin si elena saints and archangels nicula, mid-19th century 21 may the theme of this icon is saints constantine and helen, the emperors. gaius flavius valerius aurelius constantinus (born 272/274 – died may 337), also known as constantine i or constantine the great, was roman emperor from 306 to 337, becoming ruler of the whole roman empire after defeating maxentius and licinius. flavia julia helena (248–329), the wife of the roman general constantius chlorus, was the mother of the holy emperor constantine the great. she was a woman of great faith, known for her piety. she made a pilgrimage to palestine and the eastern provinces, and tradition credits her with finding the holy cross of christ and the remains of the three magi. the feast of saints constantine and helen is one of the most important for christians, because emperor constantine freed them from pagan persecution (by the edict of milan, in 313), and all his work, guided by the counsel of his mother helen, was devoted to protecting the new religion. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v6": "the table of paradise masa raiului the table of paradise nicula, first half of the 19th century typical of the nicula area is the icon of “the table of paradise”, showing a rhombus-shaped table with the virgin mary, the saviour jesus christ and two saints. in this icon (after a model from the first half of the 19th century), the two saints are saint nicholas and saint paraskeva. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v5": "the annunciation buna vestire the mother of god nicula, mid-19th century 25 march the theme of this icon is the annunciation, celebrated by the orthodox church every year on 25 march: the day on which the holy archangel gabriel brings to earth the news of the birth of the son of god. he comes to a town in galilee called nazareth, to a virgin betrothed to a man named joseph, and announces to her that she will give birth to the messiah. the virgin's name was mary – the holy virgin mary. the good news given to mankind about the incarnation of the son of god in fact completes our personal feast, our own annunciation. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v4": "saint nicholas the hierarch sfantul ierarh nicolae saints and archangels cartisoara, 1894 6 december every year on 6 december, the faithful celebrate one of the most beloved saints, saint nicholas. he is also called “the wonderworker” for the many miracles he worked even during his lifetime. there are many legends about saint nicholas, and several customs and traditions are linked to his day. the best known is the giving of gifts: on the eve of the feast, 5 december, children (and adults too – why not?) put their boots by the window or the door, and saint nicholas fills them with gifts. to the naughtiest, though, he brings a little switch. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v3": "saint paraskeva sfanta cuvioasa parascheva saints and archangels nicula, 19th century 14 october the theme of this icon is saint paraskeva the new, or paraskeva of iasi, a saint honoured throughout the orthodox church, especially in romania, serbia, greece and bulgaria. in romania she is considered the protector of moldavia and is the most popular of all the saints whose relics lie in the country. hundreds of parish churches are dedicated to her. among the people she is also known as saint friday. her feast is on 14 october, when tens of thousands of people come to iasi every year to venerate her holy relics. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v2": "saint elijah the prophet sfantul proroc ilie saints and archangels 20 july on 20 july the romanian orthodox church celebrates the ascent into heaven of the holy great prophet elijah the tishbite (he came from tishbe). one of the most important prophets of the old testament, saint elijah is honoured as a great wonderworker and bringer of rain in times of drought. depicted in icons either at the mouth of his cave, fed by a raven, or in the chariot of fire in which he was taken up to heaven, the holy great prophet elijah is, in the church calendar and in folk tradition, the old testament figure most familiar to the christian conscience, and the new testament suggests that he will be the forerunner of the second coming of jesus. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v10": "the holy archangels michael and gabriel sfintii arhangheli mihail si gavriil saints and archangels maierii (alba iulia), first half of the 19th century 8 november the theme of this icon is the feast of the holy archangels michael (“the power of god”) and gabriel (“man of god”), set in the byzantine calendar on 8 november and in the latin calendar on 29 september. these saints are the patrons of many churches, known as the leaders of the choirs of angels, the guardians of people from birth to death and the guides of souls on their way to paradise. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v1": "the nativity of the lord nasterea domnului jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, late 18th century 25 december the theme of this icon (nicula, late 18th century) is the nativity of the lord. on 25 december christians all over the world celebrate christmas, the feast of the nativity of the lord. more than two thousand years ago, the virgin mary (by the power of the holy spirit) gave birth to the child jesus in bethlehem of judea, in a poor manger. then the three magi from the east saw a bright star in the sky and, travelling a long way to follow it, reached bethlehem, bringing the saviour gifts of gold, myrrh and frankincense. christmas as we know it today dates from the year 325; until then, pre-christian religions marked the winter solstice at the same time of year. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v21": "adam and eve in paradise adam si eva in rai jesus christ and the great feasts nicula, second half of the 19th century according to the book of genesis (the first book of the old testament and of the bible), adam and eve were the first man and the first woman created by god. the moment when the two break the divine commandment and taste from the tree of knowledge is a frequent theme in iconography. this theme also attracted the transylvanian icon painters, who painted the famous old testament scene on glass. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v20": "jesus christ – the true vine iisus hristos – vita de vie jesus christ and the great feasts scheii brasovului, mid-19th century jesus – the true vine is a theme found in the transylvanian peasant icons, evoking the mystery of holy communion. the icon illustrates the parable of the vine: “i am the vine, you are the branches”. jesus presented himself as the true vine, his father as the vinedresser who planted it, and his disciples as the branches of this vine. it is an archetype according to which the essential elements of life – food, healing and worship – grew out of the primordial sacrifice. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade.", "v19": "the holy apostles peter and paul sfintii apostoli petru si pavel saints and archangels nicula, early 19th century 29 june in orthodox iconography, saints peter and paul (the first and the last among the apostles) stand for the church, or the communion of israel (peter) with all the peoples of the world (paul). the model of the church held up by the two saints illustrates the words of jesus: “you are peter, and on this rock i will build my church”. hand-painted on glass in tempera and gold leaf, over a pen-and-ink drawing made after the original model. the stained fir frame is also handmade."};
